{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/people.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:19:13.450723Z","id":"d774bf8a61470a5710397d813a95e22f90179cb072f7ee0454134c093b81c55f","body":{"detail":"release_unconnected (now crates/clax-store/src/people.rs:2363) no longer releases a person who redeemed an invite (a hosted daemon's browser redeems one without a grant; 5274dba44) or who has a GitHub identity (dfe4b35d3). Store::grants_next_due (line 2109) now names an unredeemed invite's lapse, one second after its expires_at, so the sweep releases its person then rather than at the next periodic sweep (1fc405b97). The release still sets person = 0 and rights_json = NULL with no person.rights event, and the lapse itself records nothing: the record's concern stands at the moved lines.","kind":"comment","references":"05ca3c90a72b9254238c8d4ff6ac2fdff13d731d1a21261c0e67eac9642a67cd","summary":"Changed since recorded: fewer people are released, and a lapse is acted on when it happens; neither the lapse nor the release is recorded yet","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:19:13.450916Z","id":"2bc16a1ffb9ca8e43723b87ae31b78f9082230a6adaeacf7dcaa603c77088e1f","body":{"detail":"6704086a6 rewrote reaper_ends_only_idle_sessions_with_dead_or_unknown_pids (now crates/clax-store/src/sessions.rs:2297-2333) as the suggested fix asks: the store is test_util::store_with_clock(ManualClock::at(\"2026-09-01T10:00:00Z\")), the test advances the clock 301 s instead of std::thread::sleep(300 ms), and reap_sessions runs with a 300 s idle limit, so `fresh` is not idle however loaded the machine is. Not closed here: the record is main's.","kind":"comment","references":"9daba4912ee6d6dfc47850bd226691e02de2be5246e18c7cabb1f19500a18299","summary":"Fixed on this branch: the reaper test runs on an injected clock and sleeps no more; proposed close (reason fixed)","tags":["flaky-test","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:07:03.986308Z","id":"53d8fb26f896fee66590251760eb4e7e44df6ce88c874f26fb24b3422982111e","body":{"detail":"Copies of migrations 24 and 25 from 2026-10-10 (git log -S page_person -- crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs: ddfff6383, 051681542, 86fcda318, 4b6a1d656) add versions.page_person and comments.page_person, which the final migrations replace with versions.by_page/file_authors_json and page_authors. repair() does not drop or carry them: no code reads them, the meaning of their values does not map onto page_authors rows one for one, and only development homes of that week can hold them. Such a home keeps two dead nullable columns, so its schema differs from a new one's by them. tests/fixtures/old-migrations holds no fixture of that shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1481},"end":{"line":1535},"content_hash":"928042f66c850e8ea90b44e60bbd252daca90b7cf4434d3a220ab157eeaa8ac2"},"summary":"Migration 37's repair leaves comments.page_person and versions.page_person where an early multi-person build added them","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by a 2026-10-10 multi-person build is still in use","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:07:03.986467Z","id":"fa745f606c9055872b699176fe9818078c10186833a94c16971e0e79f18e59ec","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home whose user_version is 29 and whose migration 29 was 98b628173's device publishing (crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs blob c196df9e8, branch rust-int, 2026-10-14T01:08) fails Store::open with 'table device_codes already exists' when the current migration 30 runs. The next commit, b8015c192 two minutes later, renumbered it, so only a home opened by that one build is affected. Migration 37 cannot reach it; a fix would have to change migration 30 (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) or detect the shape before it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1114},"end":{"line":1130},"content_hash":"68c376ab25c5adbecd810ad5d5460206150cc8eea0ae13e01d8925b1b44388a5"},"summary":"A database left at schema 29 by rust-int commit 98b628173 fails migration 30 before migration 37 can repair it","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by rust-int commit 98b628173 is reported","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:07:03.986562Z","id":"5c74e449554814d7920430d1d7d493fea8fdd64a20534e25b32b25cb5cc1ec7f","body":{"detail":"rust-int commit c308495e6 (2026-10-14) made push_approvals without upto (NOT NULL, no default), so the table is rebuilt. No version is recorded for such a row; 0 approves none, where the artifact's current version could approve one the owner never saw. Only a local daemon writes push_approvals, so a hosted database has no such rows. Tested by migrations::tests::repair::migration_37_carries_inbox_items_and_push_approvals_through_their_rebuilds.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1346},"end":{"line":1351},"content_hash":"8e82eb74502c4778d5b82adb86e36b45a5abfb6246d88681ff24f0b686d20fcb"},"summary":"Migration 37 keeps a push_approvals row that lacks upto with upto = 0, so its push asks the owner again","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T18:56:07.897683Z","id":"28a9474386f523910274883c115bd15164bcd869f107033269adcd36951edcba","body":{"detail":"Store::note_delivery keeps delivered_written_at only for a comment with author_kind 'viewer', via_page = 0 and author_public_id equal to the session's person (else the owner's public ID). A page writing through the comments capability may do so without the person's input, so its time is left out; the delivery still places the question. Not taken: counting via_page comments by their author_public_id like hand-written ones.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"aa65147c5240be1bf3f96347a7648545424a0791a5cadd4bff56664d6da32391"},"summary":"A comment a page wrote as the person (via_page) is not the person's Clax activity","tags":["revisit:pages write comments only on the person's own action and those deliveries are suggested as the terminal wrongly","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:22:17.260933Z","id":"ada756fec31a27fb10d6cdc96be0ceee2c3ec8e9ac9e109187c996dee7dba619","body":{"detail":"Store::note_answer keeps the question's pulled_at, else closed_at, as delivered_written_at, so clax_core::surface::suggest weighs it against the last terminal prompt (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs late_answers). Only the question's recipient, the session's person, can answer, skip or pull (Store::question_of in crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs owner_close), so it is their own act. It includes an answer through the token from no browser (answered_via cli), which is the person but not in a Clax tab.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":151},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"292cbdda1ba104c7e133fdce0b41b673c0f4a213b4bae9b2c921cb50d9540c58"},"summary":"An answer, skip or Ask me here handed over counts as the person's Clax activity at the time they acted; the path not taken lets it only place the suggestion, as a delivered comment by another author does","tags":["revisit:answers with answered_via cli become common, or the owner wants a delivery never to count as activity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.494227Z","id":"753afb8fe5f0467633ea947700911537d845fadb18712600b7630c60b268e599","body":{"detail":"Store::note_delivery keeps delivered_written_at only for a comment with author_kind 'viewer', via_page = 0 and author_public_id equal to the session's person (else the owner's public ID). A page writing through the comments capability may do so without the person's input, so its time is left out; the delivery still places the question. Not taken: counting via_page comments by their author_public_id like hand-written ones.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":141},"end":{"line":148},"content_hash":"aa65147c5240be1bf3f96347a7648545424a0791a5cadd4bff56664d6da32391"},"summary":"A comment a page wrote as the person (via_page) is not the person's Clax activity","supersedes":"28a9474386f523910274883c115bd15164bcd869f107033269adcd36951edcba","tags":["revisit:pages write comments only on the person's own action and those deliveries are suggested as the terminal wrongly","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T19:41:40.517315Z","id":"84297a70fa901d940ed3dcee23ef49d3227940fd0c0ee18f6f5b08c8acb765f8","body":{"detail":"Store::note_answer keeps the question's pulled_at, else closed_at, as delivered_written_at, and what the person did as delivered_act, so clax_core::surface::suggest weighs it against the last terminal prompt (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs late_answers). A question about no artifact (an inbox question) sets only the act and delivered_since_turn, leaving the last delivery's time and place. Only the question's recipient, the session's person, can answer, skip or pull (Store::question_of in crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs owner_close), so it is their own act. It includes an answer through the token from no browser (answered_via cli), which is the person but not in a Clax tab.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":162},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"eabddad981a8df370ada43c1e699e0491d2c7bccbdd43884610b9e9989e731e2"},"summary":"An answer, skip or Ask me here handed over counts as the person's Clax activity at the time they acted; the path not taken lets it only place the suggestion, as a delivered comment by another author does","supersedes":"ada756fec31a27fb10d6cdc96be0ceee2c3ec8e9ac9e109187c996dee7dba619","tags":["revisit:answers with answered_via cli become common, or the owner wants a delivery never to count as activity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:16:44.619513Z","id":"0011b8fec69bbb2514b15bb8b49844b3c6033d360c141a4e637cd66d375908d8","body":{"detail":"scan_linked_questions pairs a thread question as any other ask question; its thread_id is this daemon's, not the remote's, so it is not sent and the remote's copy is about the artifact only. The person answering on the remote finds it on the artifact, not beside the thread it was asked in. linked threads already map local threads to remote ones (linked_thread_by_remote and the linked threads table in crates/clax-store/src/linked.rs); mapping the question's thread through them is follow-up work.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1169},"end":{"line":1178},"content_hash":"39044e6116fa5b5932368d2128ba4a549be578a9fdf67bd650fd81a07da2a15c"},"suggested_fix":"When the question's thread has a linked twin on the remote, send the twin's remote thread ID with the copy.","summary":"A thread question about a linked artifact is copied to the remote without its thread, so the person sees it on the remote's artifact, not in the linked thread","tags":["linked","follow-up","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.662735Z","id":"0c155fcd8e655a7c43a62957f3e932a2edfb616520d5bb95bf78b5a0579db831","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1363-1368, record 0118687f.\n\nconnection_decided reads a connection item only when the owner approves or denies the request (crates/clax-core/src/store/people.rs approve_grant, deny_grant). A pending request that expires after 10 minutes (request_grant's stale sweep, expire_grants) leaves its item unread in the owner's inbox; once the unapproved row is purged a day later the item renders gone with connection null. Reading it at the lapse, or touching it so the shell shows the expired status, would need the lapse paths to call into the inbox.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1392},"end":{"line":1397},"content_hash":"c1c86e26871ba066020c75f1d9b1b954ee91add027a8fb30f98694a07930d59d"},"summary":"A connection request that lapses unanswered keeps its connection item unread","supersedes":"314e74125566ec5319b77e5147b3d9c691e9447f003f345a0aee05b1a3640100","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/inbox.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.685392Z","id":"1633743c8a4457821492d2020d40038c1e265dd77dcbce8d60462a827c5176cb","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/inbox.rs:1552-1556, record 6014047e.\n\nnote_finished makes the finished item for the session's person. A first publish by a person's agent reaches both the person and the owner (note_version), since a new artifact appears in the owner's gallery; finished work was left to the person, per spec §18 ('Inbox, questions: own').","kind":"alternative","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1596},"end":{"line":1600},"content_hash":"df46c2781c4e06aa0fe53e6fadd564b9bcbcad9e060403b47de165ac7d60413a"},"summary":"A connected person's agent's finished work reaches its person only, not the owner","supersedes":"c4826cf52130d479a045154c976c46d2696e038062c532f03e396310f92b7e10","tags":["revisit:the owner asks to follow other people's agents' work in their inbox","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T20:21:07.708020Z","id":"0e4f092370e31dcb4f89bb6cf9a6af26d09b32d88d9d0182e1eeab2a0b372ac6","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/mod.rs:757-783, record 102e3b6a.\n\nMeasured on this machine (load average about 45): the clax-core lib tests take 12.4 s with --skip the_store_tests_pass_on_one_connection and 20.8 s with it, since the child runs 455 tests after the parent's. The threshold `passed > 300` passes with 455; a module dropped from the filter (or from test_util::store) loses its coverage on one connection without failing it.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":768},"end":{"line":794},"content_hash":"b3bfd31319c95da4542d5ac7bd7f9fa165b3082f4e9534f5f055a9a24bdcbbee"},"suggested_fix":"Compare `passed` against the count the same filter lists (`--list`) less the ignored ones, or pin the module set.","summary":"The one-connection rerun adds about 8 s to the clax-core unit suite, and its >300 threshold only catches an empty filter","supersedes":"fb83a7fe7afcd453363b4e3fdfa4b0d1ca2b6a3eb8d48bce7df5277bfe4d7ac5","tags":["wasm","gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.025487Z","id":"977cc9bedd231bad3ad63bf29481d3099b05bac1c554f02742c8a5d411ed9a3d","body":{"detail":"note_terminal withdraws (reason lapsed) only open in-terminal questions with source hook. An in-terminal question the agent posted with ask {in_terminal: true} before asking in chat closes only when the agent cancels it, though in Claude Code and Pi the person's chat answer is a typed prompt the daemon sees (prompt hook, Pi's input event). A forgotten cancel leaves a terminal card and an unread inbox item until the session ends. Lapsing them on a reported prompt (never on an inferred turn, crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs note_turn and note_turn_start) would close them; it is not done because a prompt may be about something else while the agent's chat question still waits.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"b4c9466cbf477911beaf5251c905aa8798afb73103a9dfa37e7705d47bfbfe8d"},"summary":"Lapse an agent's own in-terminal ask question too at a reported prompt, not only a hook question","tags":["revisit:terminal cards of ask in-terminal questions are seen left open after the person answered in chat","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.025529Z","id":"f446dfbcb45c60dfece009a5852a194db92136ff58af5fc8aab6705c155758f7","body":{"detail":"The UPDATE of sessions.terminal_at runs in one with_tx, the read of the open hook in-terminal questions in a with_read, and each close_question in its own transaction. A hook question created between the stamp and the read is lapsed by this prompt though it was asked after it; one created after the read survives this prompt and lapses at the next. Both are narrow races between a prompt and an AskUserQuestion of the same session.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":84},"content_hash":"b4c9466cbf477911beaf5251c905aa8798afb73103a9dfa37e7705d47bfbfe8d"},"suggested_fix":"Stamp the prompt and select the questions to lapse in one transaction, keeping only questions created before the stamp.","summary":"note_terminal stamps the prompt and lapses hook in-terminal questions in separate transactions","tags":["race","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.025564Z","id":"4fb2952084745a4a24f0a0e728d65c8daeef382fdde585e0c6df204b58cdf7dd","body":{"detail":"note_answer for a question about no artifact (an inbox question) sets only delivered_written_at, delivered_act and delivered_since_turn, leaving delivered_at, delivered_artifact_id and delivered_thread_id of the last placed delivery. clax_core::surface::place_of (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs:144-155) then places the suggestion at that older delivery's thread whenever it is newer than the last terminal prompt, so after the person answers an inbox question the agent may be told to ask in a thread the current work did not come from.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":218},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"d547c4e1bc84b78f5740738ec8cd6d932c6d1c4ffc5deedde9475eb8df869f21"},"suggested_fix":"Have an inbox act clear the delivered place (or record that the last delivery placed nothing), so place_of falls back to the session's page.","summary":"An inbox act after a newer placed delivery keeps the old delivery's thread as the suggestion's where","tags":["where-to-ask","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.262802Z","id":"0136dfba6bffdc1b9e7a23531107f1d53aafc59dd41e40b41d50c9209d2339f0","body":{"detail":"Store::note_delivery keeps delivered_written_at only for a comment with author_kind 'viewer', via_page = 0 and author_public_id equal to the session's person (else the owner's public ID). A page writing through the comments capability may do so without the person's input, so its time is left out; the delivery still places the question. Not taken: counting via_page comments by their author_public_id like hand-written ones.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":189},"end":{"line":196},"content_hash":"aa65147c5240be1bf3f96347a7648545424a0791a5cadd4bff56664d6da32391"},"summary":"A comment a page wrote as the person (via_page) is not the person's Clax activity","supersedes":"753afb8fe5f0467633ea947700911537d845fadb18712600b7630c60b268e599","tags":["revisit:pages write comments only on the person's own action and those deliveries are suggested as the terminal wrongly","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:06:54.285266Z","id":"e6e2e634eabc17cc0e496c32d8aba5bb49d97b497d0381b2d37de1121ce0f95c","body":{"detail":"Store::note_answer keeps the question's pulled_at, else closed_at, as delivered_written_at, and what the person did as delivered_act, so clax_core::surface::suggest weighs it against the last terminal prompt (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs late_answers). A question about no artifact (an inbox question) sets only the act and delivered_since_turn, leaving the last delivery's time and place. Only the question's recipient, the session's person, can answer, skip or pull (Store::question_of in crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs owner_close), so it is their own act. It includes an answer through the token from no browser (answered_via cli), which is the person but not in a Clax tab.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":210},"end":{"line":244},"content_hash":"eabddad981a8df370ada43c1e699e0491d2c7bccbdd43884610b9e9989e731e2"},"summary":"An answer, skip or Ask me here handed over counts as the person's Clax activity at the time they acted; the path not taken lets it only place the suggestion, as a delivered comment by another author does","supersedes":"84297a70fa901d940ed3dcee23ef49d3227940fd0c0ee18f6f5b08c8acb765f8","tags":["revisit:answers with answered_via cli become common, or the owner wants a delivery never to count as activity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/site.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:27:19.349179Z","id":"d7065ed49427f9738d394cfde45d2ebf6d55f88822379e796bf31db14a437d7c","body":{"detail":"commit_refile moves questions.artifact_id (and sessions.delivered_artifact_id) to the thread's new page in the re-filing transaction, but no question event is published for them: Store::refile_threads has no app state to call clax_http::views::question::announce_thread. An open page keeps such a question's old artifact (its link and where it is listed) until web/shell/src/q/feed.svelte.ts fetches the questions again (ready or resync).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":704},"end":{"line":713},"content_hash":"54900b3164a1ac130b08100f5cb0e5ac2d6271bc8789ea682d48a0c3bb528adc"},"suggested_fix":"Return the moved thread IDs from refile_threads to its callers (the routes and the join), and have them call announce_thread for each.","summary":"A re-filed thread's questions reach an open page only at its next fetch of the questions","tags":["ui","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:27:19.349290Z","id":"645c38edc3a04ec609ba8c7f3d8e2379cc1515956223c2057aaf1a34668421c3","body":{"detail":"Store::note_queued keeps a Codex queue delivery for the next turn (queued_since_turn) only while turn_open is set, which note_turn_start sets at any poll but stop_hook and queue and note_turn clears. Three cases are not exact: a push that lands in a turn that has made no tool call yet is taken as idle, so the open turn's Stop clears the delivery and the queued turn's first poll is inferred typed; a turn whose Stop hook never ran (an interrupted turn) leaves turn_open set, so an idle push is kept past the pushed turn's end and the next typed turn is taken as Clax's; and the push records its delivery after `codex queue` exits (crates/clax-realtime/src/push.rs dispatch), so a queued turn that polls first is inferred typed. The working records in clax-realtime were not used: they follow artifacts, not turns.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":174},"end":{"line":189},"content_hash":"5b4205b18c80bb4782b3fddd2bd010d619ff6ff5c38e961923d925351492d7c0"},"summary":"Tell a busy Codex session from an idle one by an open turn (a non-Stop poll since the last Stop); the residue is a turn with no tool call yet, a Stop that never came, and a queued turn that polls before codex queue exits","tags":["revisit:Codex reports turn starts (a hook or app-server event), or where-to-ask is seen naming the terminal for a pushed turn","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:27:19.372871Z","id":"b22ef8b6de6ce36d08862aad6946ac6216ce1fe192467b2fe6ff874b9a942004","body":{"detail":"note_answer for a question about no artifact (an inbox question) sets only delivered_written_at, delivered_act and delivered_since_turn, leaving delivered_at, delivered_artifact_id and delivered_thread_id of the last placed delivery. clax_core::surface::place_of (crates/clax-core/src/surface.rs:144-155) then places the suggestion at that older delivery's thread whenever it is newer than the last terminal prompt, so after the person answers an inbox question the agent may be told to ask in a thread the current work did not come from.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":235},"end":{"line":261},"content_hash":"d547c4e1bc84b78f5740738ec8cd6d932c6d1c4ffc5deedde9475eb8df869f21"},"suggested_fix":"Have an inbox act clear the delivered place (or record that the last delivery placed nothing), so place_of falls back to the session's page.","summary":"An inbox act after a newer placed delivery keeps the old delivery's thread as the suggestion's where","supersedes":"4fb2952084745a4a24f0a0e728d65c8daeef382fdde585e0c6df204b58cdf7dd","tags":["where-to-ask","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:27:19.395705Z","id":"724eb8eca7f90cf7a69bcdae129f3d2451f98030b55a719f04f92fcccffba3c9","body":{"detail":"Store::note_delivery keeps delivered_written_at only for a comment with author_kind 'viewer', via_page = 0 and author_public_id equal to the session's person (else the owner's public ID). A page writing through the comments capability may do so without the person's input, so its time is left out; the delivery still places the question. Not taken: counting via_page comments by their author_public_id like hand-written ones.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":206},"end":{"line":213},"content_hash":"aa65147c5240be1bf3f96347a7648545424a0791a5cadd4bff56664d6da32391"},"summary":"A comment a page wrote as the person (via_page) is not the person's Clax activity","supersedes":"0136dfba6bffdc1b9e7a23531107f1d53aafc59dd41e40b41d50c9209d2339f0","tags":["revisit:pages write comments only on the person's own action and those deliveries are suggested as the terminal wrongly","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/engagement.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T21:27:19.417962Z","id":"156301e732d067fefedf019a94e8da3fb8933280580cdf14281beca4539fafd0","body":{"detail":"Store::note_answer keeps the question's pulled_at, else closed_at, as delivered_written_at, and what the person did as delivered_act, so clax_core::surface::suggest weighs it against the last terminal prompt (crates/clax-server/src/routes/feedback.rs late_answers). A question about no artifact (an inbox question) sets only the act and delivered_since_turn, leaving the last delivery's time and place. Only the question's recipient, the session's person, can answer, skip or pull (Store::question_of in crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs owner_close), so it is their own act. It includes an answer through the token from no browser (answered_via cli), which is the person but not in a Clax tab.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":227},"end":{"line":261},"content_hash":"eabddad981a8df370ada43c1e699e0491d2c7bccbdd43884610b9e9989e731e2"},"summary":"An answer, skip or Ask me here handed over counts as the person's Clax activity at the time they acted; the path not taken lets it only place the suggestion, as a delivered comment by another author does","supersedes":"e6e2e634eabc17cc0e496c32d8aba5bb49d97b497d0381b2d37de1121ce0f95c","tags":["revisit:answers with answered_via cli become common, or the owner wants a delivery never to count as activity","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:14:24.865219Z","id":"00c6643bdb6839bef67db1331c2989054334da8a66fef43507e1dde5156967d6","body":{"detail":"Failure: a home whose user_version is 29 and whose migration 29 was 98b628173's device publishing (crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs blob c196df9e8, branch rust-int, 2026-10-14T01:08) fails Store::open with 'table device_codes already exists' when the current migration 30 runs. The next commit, b8015c192 two minutes later, renumbered it, so only a home opened by that one build is affected. Migration 37 cannot reach it; a fix would have to change migration 30 (CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS) or detect the shape before it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1114},"end":{"line":1129},"content_hash":"2b824f6033e11d7da18d8730e9656465a8171749c6546b89674f0c4a734d95ad"},"summary":"A database left at schema 29 by rust-int commit 98b628173 fails migration 30 before migration 37 can repair it","supersedes":"fa745f606c9055872b699176fe9818078c10186833a94c16971e0e79f18e59ec","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by rust-int commit 98b628173 is reported","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:14:24.900438Z","id":"b7e429cbb788218dcb929923f327ebcb3e2ba16c8d91617b26d70c5ee85036cf","body":{"detail":"rust-int commit c308495e6 (2026-10-14) made push_approvals without upto (NOT NULL, no default), so the table is rebuilt. No version is recorded for such a row; 0 approves none, where the artifact's current version could approve one the owner never saw. Only a local daemon writes push_approvals, so a hosted database has no such rows. Tested by migrations::tests::repair::migration_37_carries_inbox_items_and_push_approvals_through_their_rebuilds.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1382},"end":{"line":1387},"content_hash":"8e82eb74502c4778d5b82adb86e36b45a5abfb6246d88681ff24f0b686d20fcb"},"summary":"Migration 37 keeps a push_approvals row that lacks upto with upto = 0, so its push asks the owner again","supersedes":"5c74e449554814d7920430d1d7d493fea8fdd64a20534e25b32b25cb5cc1ec7f","tags":["migrations","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T03:14:24.933747Z","id":"4717eb4eec3e51168f8b9ae20f459f5d18c962be9ade6236a718c9d53a9ada9e","body":{"detail":"Copies of migrations 24 and 25 from 2026-10-10 (git log -S page_person -- crates/clax-core/src/store/migrations.rs: ddfff6383, 051681542, 86fcda318, 4b6a1d656) add versions.page_person and comments.page_person, which the final migrations replace with versions.by_page/file_authors_json and page_authors. repair() does not drop or carry them: no code reads them, the meaning of their values does not map onto page_authors rows one for one, and only development homes of that week can hold them. Such a home keeps two dead nullable columns, so its schema differs from a new one's by them. tests/fixtures/old-migrations holds no fixture of that shape.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1517},"end":{"line":1571},"content_hash":"928042f66c850e8ea90b44e60bbd252daca90b7cf4434d3a220ab157eeaa8ac2"},"summary":"Migration 37's repair leaves comments.page_person and versions.page_person where an early multi-person build added them","supersedes":"53d8fb26f896fee66590251760eb4e7e44df6ce88c874f26fb24b3422982111e","tags":["migrations","revisit:a home made by a 2026-10-10 multi-person build is still in use","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T12:19:34.874165Z","id":"df2ff62d50ea342b3df5b4436489b05a1bb6fbcafa6ba35f44b8d06327cdcfbc","body":{"detail":"Earlier flutter-app builds numbered the app migrations from 24 (no invites table) and, after the multi-person rebase, from 27 (invites, no hosted_setup). adopt_earlier_flutter_app runs the migrations such a database lacks below 38 (24 to 26 for the first kind, then 27 to 37) and sets user_version to 37 + n. Migration 37's repair (REPAIR_TABLES, REPAIR_COLUMNS, REPAIR_INDEXES) makes every object the removed repair_multi_person_revisions added (viewer_cookies with legacy cookies, approval_requests_by_target and _by_thread, feedback.no_access_at), so an adopted database of the earlier multi-person revision reaches the final schema through it. Tests: migrations::tests::a_database_at_the_earlier_app_numbering_31_keeps_every_row_and_is_copied_first, databases_at_the_earlier_app_numbering_27_to_30_upgrade, a_database_of_the_earlier_multi_person_revision_gets_the_final_schema_and_keeps_its_rows. An adopted database's artifacts table has the app's columns before the base's (column order differs from a fresh database; shape_of compares up to order).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1263},"end":{"line":1309},"content_hash":"ff906a2d65a74dba18f1184ad72919e975f88a2856c28da8b620d01277baab3d"},"summary":"The app's migrations are 38 to 42 after akesling/clax-artifacts's 27 to 37; databases of both earlier flutter-app numberings are adopted here by schema","tags":["migrations","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-18T12:19:34.874526Z","id":"89ea1abf01b86c95266b5c54ebac8e7fb9734be7e8fd1f514c36d3382112b44f","body":{"detail":"The content store's VersionWrite carries files only from the version before (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs), so restore_version_async reads version n's bytes and puts them; the audit record still names only unchanged files as carried (VersionStep::Restore). An artifact with large files costs their whole size per restore; a carry-from-version in ContentStore would avoid it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1142},"end":{"line":1217},"content_hash":"9b9fca69fdcb856c0931947f11776a4816b06f4ca3ad3abf3d31268b6a811ecb"},"summary":"A restore reads every file of the restored version into memory and writes them all again as the new version's puts","tags":["restore","content","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T04:12:28.607681Z","id":"b79e68dedf116715ea171f76c54f6ce3eee8840af63364e3dfdf9383e2c816e1","body":{"detail":"Earlier flutter-app builds numbered the app migrations from 24 (no invites table), then from 27 (invites, no hosted_setup), then from 38 (hosted_setup, no questions.thread_id). adopt_earlier_flutter_app runs the migrations such a database lacks below APP_MIGRATION (39): 24 to 26 for the first kind, 27 to 37 for the first two, and WHERE_TO_ASK_MIGRATION (38) for all three; it then sets user_version to 38 + n. A database at 38 to 42 in the from-38 numbering is recognised by db_read_grants without questions.thread_id. Migration 37's repair (REPAIR_TABLES, REPAIR_COLUMNS, REPAIR_INDEXES) makes every object the removed repair_multi_person_revisions added, so an adopted database of the earlier multi-person revision reaches the final schema through it. Tests: migrations::tests::databases_at_the_app_numbering_from_38_upgrade_with_every_row_and_a_copy_first, an_app_numbering_from_38_database_whose_schema_disagrees_with_its_version_is_left_alone, a_database_at_the_earlier_app_numbering_31_keeps_every_row_and_is_copied_first, databases_at_the_earlier_app_numbering_27_to_30_upgrade, pre_rebase_flutter_app_databases_at_24_to_26_upgrade. An adopted database's tables can have the app's columns before the base's (column order differs from a fresh database; shape_of compares up to order).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":1278},"end":{"line":1353},"content_hash":"fbb970d49b5791fe81e9fba7217be8defa904d8f9c8d972bc42f220b37767356"},"summary":"The app's migrations are 39 to 43, after main's where-to-ask migration 38; databases of the three earlier flutter-app numberings (from 24, 27 and 38) are adopted here by schema","supersedes":"df2ff62d50ea342b3df5b4436489b05a1bb6fbcafa6ba35f44b8d06327cdcfbc","tags":["migrations","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:43:09.520920Z","id":"3014bcd2b445b6f10542c1d452ca06d7a147eb36169eaa675d1a1465db5fffc9","body":{"detail":"See APP_MIGRATION, MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38 and adopt_earlier_flutter_app's doc comment (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs:1286-1412). This record's summary names 39 to 43 and three layouts; it wants re-recording or closing by its owner.","kind":"comment","references":"b79e68dedf116715ea171f76c54f6ce3eee8840af63364e3dfdf9383e2c816e1","summary":"Out of date since 4479a586c: the app's migrations are now 41 to 45, after main's 39 and 40, and a fourth earlier layout (the app's at 39 to 43) is adopted","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:43:09.521128Z","id":"a658f3eb1f2c8a93d9fca1cf0fbbfaf5c116c73c28baac0d8761da3456dfe27f","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-store/tests/fixtures/old-migrations/flutter-app-4508df19f.sql replays the old migrations' SQL with rows the tests insert. A dump of a real schema-43 home (crates/clax-embed/tests/fixtures/homes/flutter-app-43.sql) and crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs, which would open it through the embedded core and check the clax-43-* backup, user_version 45 and every artifact, version, thread and comment, do not exist yet. Until they do, the open of the owner's phone and Mac homes by a build carrying this numbering is not exercised end to end; those homes are also to be copied off and opened on the Mac before any install.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1344},"end":{"line":1412},"content_hash":"622ea38f729f44b1b9db1f9cc5c7a5f7684576b21c499e40060afbc62c3a2691"},"suggested_fix":"Add the schema-43 home dump and old_homes.rs, and extend it to assert the backup, user_version 45 and the row counts.","summary":"Adoption of an installed home at 43 is tested only on a home the store's tests build from the 4508df19f fixture, not on a home written by the installed app's own clax","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:49:04.304354Z","id":"8c47eb29a6f0a7de9c605d8fdee3859decaf4c9b4d87f266001cb9a22ce10410","body":{"detail":"Main's numbering is followed by copying main's migrations and adding one mark per migration to MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38 (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 10.2: 'a later renumbering adds one mark per new main migration and nothing else'). Suppose main lands a 41 that makes table foo: the branch copies it, MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38 becomes [legal_agreements, briefs, foo] and APP_MIGRATION 42. A home this build wrote at 45 has db_read_grants, questions.thread_id, legal_agreements and briefs but not foo, so main_held is [true, true, false] and lines 1366-1370 refuse it ('holds the app's tables and only some of the migrations before them'). Without that branch it would still be refused, since the layout code (first = WHERE_TO_ASK_MIGRATION + 1) only knows the app's migrations starting at 39, and 45 is outside 39..=43. The comment at 1328-1333 says such a database 'was made by no build'; that holds only until main adds a migration. Once a build of this numbering is installed on the owner's devices, the first main merge that adds a migration breaks their next launch unless a fifth layout is written by hand, and the plan's instruction for that case (2026-10-19-in-process-core.md Task 19 Step 1) does not ask for one. Options for the owner: (a) generalise now: when questions.thread_id is present and the held main marks are a leading prefix of MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38 of length k < len, the app's migrations start at WHERE_TO_ASK_MIGRATION + 1 + k; refuse only a non-prefix pattern; (b) land the app's migrations on main before any further main migration, so their numbers stop moving; (c) keep the current code and require a fifth layout at the next renumbering.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1357},"end":{"line":1372},"content_hash":"a141b106e880b2fa4ce95fd2121db043dc67481ff6cc6a49fa3ace824a1b8292"},"suggested_fix":"Derive the app's first number from the length of the leading run of held main marks (option a) and add a test that appends a synthetic mark to MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38's role (or parameterises it) to show a home of each earlier main prefix adopts.","summary":"The next migration main adds above 40 makes every home of this numbering (at 41 to 45, or 46 after the jobs migration) refused at open","tags":["review","migrations","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:49:04.304545Z","id":"cfc2812444ea9e253b33728597428ac7a2f7bac309374422d8da33b7c61dda0e","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 10.2: 'the open is refused with MigrationFailed naming the mismatch and the backup'. The refusal detail here is 'a database from an earlier Clax app build at version N <why>; it was left unchanged'. backup::before_migrate returns the copy's path, but Store::open_with (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:270-275) discards it, so neither the error nor the app's migration-failure screen can tell the person where the copy is. The copy is logged once at warn level by before_migrate.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1351},"end":{"line":1356},"content_hash":"0e232adc8b520411b484c15b1e4618133a9496565ccda854a55ecd927d646212"},"suggested_fix":"Carry the path from before_migrate into the MigrationFailed detail (or a field of it) when the open fails after a copy was made.","summary":"A refused open names the mismatch but not the backup it made, though spec section 10.2 says the refusal names both","tags":["review","migrations","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:49:04.304592Z","id":"043c7c85e37cdcd2eb3a9a8bffb117864804808fc8d03474dc23d22e54b5143f","body":{"detail":"VACUUM INTO does not fsync the file it writes (SQLite's documentation for VACUUM INTO says so), and the rename at line 55 is not followed by an fsync of the file or of backups/. The migrations that follow commit with SQLite's own syncs. A power loss or OS crash (not a process kill) right after an adoption or migration commits can leave the database migrated and the copy missing or torn. The adoption of the installed homes adds tables only (main's 39 and 40), so the copy is a safety net rather than the only source of the rows, which bounds the harm today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":51},"end":{"line":55},"content_hash":"b2f82bc099087cae91613a4ed6380ceed0e12bd87c60f2ca7301ff2117fd3355"},"suggested_fix":"Open the temporary copy and call File::sync_all before the rename, then sync the backups directory after it.","summary":"The pre-migration copy is not synced to disk before the migration that follows it commits","tags":["review","backup","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:49:04.304713Z","id":"2e0dcbbc9668cfa590524eca9f1b7fd742192590e85795935909317adbb70677","body":{"detail":"installed_at_43 and the DROP TABLE run on connections that close before the bytes are read, so the WAL is checkpointed and the main file is final. The owner's Mac homes each carried about 800 KB of WAL frames when copied (clax.db-wal of 815792 and 832272 bytes). On a refusal the store's connection closes as the last one, and SQLite checkpoints those frames into clax.db, so its bytes change while its content stays as it was. The guarantee worth asserting is the schema and every row (every_row) of the database before and after, with the WAL holding frames when the open starts.","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":4553},"end":{"line":4579},"content_hash":"62d58ee88854c6e25d8186ea22c346674a776f81c6af1a97a0e516beaccd7486"},"summary":"The refusal test's byte-for-byte check holds because its home has no uncheckpointed WAL frames; a real home's file is left logically unchanged, not byte-identical","tags":["review","migrations","tests","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T02:49:04.305097Z","id":"8993b1d3e2d6a9c27534c17ed17fbde49a3e6376bea6636a1fcc7a449cbb68ac","body":{"detail":"Each clax.db with its -wal and -shm was copied with cp from a home no process held (lsof empty), then sqlite3 .backup into a scratch home with the artifacts/ directory copied; PRAGMA integrity_check ok. bazel-bin/crates/clax-cli/clax serve --foreground --port 0 with CLAX_HOME on each copy logged 'upgrading the database; copied it first from=43 to=45' then 'renumbered a database from an earlier Clax app build from=43 to=45'. Row counts per table (68 tables before, 70 after: legal_agreements and briefs added empty) were equal, and the sorted content of every pre-existing table hashed the same in the backup and the adopted database. Container home: artifacts 2, versions 18, threads 6, comments 12, docs 1, audit_events 241, inbox_items 17. Application Support home: artifacts 3, versions 7, threads 1, comments 2, docs 1, audit_events 49, inbox_items 5. GET /v/<n>/ on <id>.localhost returned 200 for all 18 and all 7 versions; GET /api/artifacts listed 2 and 3 artifacts. The phone's home and the open through the embedded core (crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs) remain unchecked, so this concern stays open.","kind":"comment","references":"a658f3eb1f2c8a93d9fca1cf0fbbfaf5c116c73c28baac0d8761da3456dfe27f","summary":"Checked at 4479a586c on copies of the owner's two Mac homes (the sandboxed container's and Application Support's clax-home): both were at user_version 43 in the 39-43 layout; this build's clax serve adopted each to 45 with a backups/clax-43-*.db copy (user_version 43) first, kept every table's rows unchanged, and served every version of every artifact","tags":["review","migrations","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.364696Z","id":"9b65e346657055319a99ad7efe7c9f8d1df88b8f7580d250a03b92c3a7493e67","body":{"detail":"Spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md §8.2 lists 'a push' among the publishes the check covers, and the Page contract text added in d223b318b (docs/contract.md 'Page contract', plugins/*/skills/clax/SKILL.md) says 'Every publish refuses one that breaks these rules'. record_push (pushes.rs:332) checks paths and sizes per file and skips the ones it cannot take, naming them in the version's note (push_note), but has no icon rule. The hosted Worker serves clax-server's router, so its HTTP publishes are checked; its pushes (RepoDO and the Artifacts queue, crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs 'Pushes') reach this function and are not.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":351},"end":{"line":378},"content_hash":"8943aa02ff98a9a26401ca3ddcdab7f4168a36e1def9df9661cc526371e8a72c"},"suggested_fix":"In the PushedContent::Bytes arm, skip a top-level icon.svg whose icon::problem is Some, as an oversize file is skipped (it lands in `skipped` and the note), and test it in the store's push tests.","summary":"A git push records a version without the icon rules: record_push builds its ValidatedPublish by hand and never calls clax_core::icon::problem, so a pushed icon.svg of any content becomes a version on the daemon and on the hosted Worker","tags":["review","icon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:18:40.364824Z","id":"2e0e9213c3e288f487326f9506ddfbc1d5e2f6d4646573f0ab3b7be9b1a2fdee","body":{"detail":"restore_version_async builds its ValidatedPublish from version n's stored files without publish::validate, so restoring a version whose icon.svg breaks a rule succeeds and the new version carries that icon (the app draws it through cleanIcon, which reads package:xml loosely). fork_artifact (crates/clax-store/src/forks.rs) copies the same way. That is the right behaviour for history, but docs/contract.md's Page contract now reads 'Every publish refuses one that breaks these rules', and a later change routing restore through validate would break restores of old versions without a failing test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1142},"end":{"line":1185},"content_hash":"4d823ffc86ba50ed5df8c7122ed05884397cae1778372f085c99ae9c025d6405"},"suggested_fix":"Add a store test that restores (and forks) a version whose icon.svg holds <script>, expecting success, and say in the contract's versions:restore and fork paragraphs that their files are not checked.","summary":"versions:restore and fork carry an icon.svg the icon rules now refuse, by design, but no test pins it and the contract does not say these paths skip the check","tags":["review","icon","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:28:46.774712Z","id":"b53e40b3f95634e82246b6245b906e141540468f210c378234736a28c780bd8b","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"8c47eb29a6f0a7de9c605d8fdee3859decaf4c9b4d87f266001cb9a22ce10410","summary":"The owner chose option (a) on 2026-10-19: where the app's migrations start in a home is derived from how many of main's marks above 38 it holds, in order (the first k gives 38 + k + 1), for any k, with no hand-written layout per renumbering and no refusal for a home this numbering left","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:28:46.775646Z","id":"064e24475a5c49903b2f9f7ba2c4ac950f46cbd5d4b449020342d05f67bda487","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f6617119b","summary":"Fixed: adopt_earlier_flutter_app takes a Numbering and starts the app's block at 38 + k + 1 for the leading run k of held main marks; APP_MIGRATION is derived from MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38; spec section 10.2 states the rule for any k. Against a simulated main 41 (with_a_main_41 in the tests), a_home_of_this_numbering_takes_a_later_main_migration_and_the_apps_renumbering (today's 45 adopts to 46 after a copy, every row kept, the later build's schema, migration 25's step not rerun, a second open changes nothing), every_layout_adopts_into_a_later_main_numbering (layouts from 24, 27, 38, 39 and 41, each app prefix) and a_home_holding_mains_later_migrations_without_an_earlier_one_is_refused pass, failing before the rule; bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all //crates/clax-core:all: both PASSED, every earlier layout's test included","supersedes":"8c47eb29a6f0a7de9c605d8fdee3859decaf4c9b4d87f266001cb9a22ce10410","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:28:47.010996Z","id":"b7e3d0e5c3c6a9b18b07903b6f7975c5902a62d7714218266f8efc318d5e871e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0867b3893","summary":"Fixed: Store::open_with keeps backup::before_migrate's path and naming_the_copy (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs) adds it to a MigrationFailed's detail. an_old_numbering_home_whose_marks_disagree_is_refused asserts the refusal names the mismatch (sample_grants) and the copy's path, and a_failing_migration_is_reported_and_rolled_back the same for a failed migration; the first failed before the change ('...lacks the table sample_grants; it was left unchanged') and both pass under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all","supersedes":"cfc2812444ea9e253b33728597428ac7a2f7bac309374422d8da33b7c61dda0e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:28:47.249181Z","id":"7640ef8a7e751ffcb60a5ec81f764484127f3f4fa7824485d6f51879ced6313c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:219733273","summary":"Fixed: before_migrate syncs the temporary copy (File::sync_all, F_FULLFSYNC on Apple platforms), renames it, then syncs backups/ (unix; a no-op elsewhere), through a Disk seam. the_copy_is_synced_then_renamed_then_its_directory_synced records the order [sync_file tmp, rename tmp, sync_dir backups] and a_copy_that_cannot_be_synced_is_not_put_in_place shows a failing step refuses the open and leaves no temporary file; both failed before the change and pass under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all. Not testable here: that the bytes survive an actual power loss, which depends on the device and filesystem honouring the syncs","supersedes":"043c7c85e37cdcd2eb3a9a8bffb117864804808fc8d03474dc23d22e54b5143f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:28:47.506230Z","id":"d398603d5e7a6bbf6b606149fef3c043032c856f191bc7bcbd3199803fc58adf","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:28c591e57","summary":"Fixed: an_old_numbering_home_whose_marks_disagree_is_refused now leaves its change in the WAL (a connection with SQLITE_DBCONFIG_NO_CKPT_ON_CLOSE and wal_autocheckpoint 0), asserts the WAL holds frames before the open, and compares user_version, schema_of and every_row before and after the refused open, and in the copy. With frames present the old byte-for-byte check failed ('left as it was'); the content check passes under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all","supersedes":"2e0dcbbc9668cfa590524eca9f1b7fd742192590e85795935909317adbb70677","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:36:04.779372Z","id":"2d8d421ad894d6ef2322b8487b230605c1f67d092f81e1d3b818154d79eacd5e","body":{"detail":"adopt_earlier_flutter_app refuses a database with db_read_grants, no questions.thread_id and legal_agreements (or any later main mark) with 'holds the table legal_agreements but lacks questions.thread_id of an earlier migration'. That string appears nowhere in the tests (grep for 'lacks questions.thread_id' in crates/clax-store matches only line 1416). The neighbouring refusal, main marks that are not a leading run, is tested by a_home_holding_mains_later_migrations_without_an_earlier_one_is_refused. Without a test, a later edit that reorders the checks (for example moving the hosted/people layout choice above this one) would run main's migrations above 38 on such a home and fail on CREATE TABLE legal_agreements, or adopt it at the wrong numbering.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1413},"end":{"line":1418},"content_hash":"470873491402e95e4122db6c94abf26930e7f167caad98fe894ff5505c3095d4"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test: build a home of the app-from-38 layout (app_numbered_from_38), add CREATE TABLE legal_agreements to it, and assert MigrationFailed naming legal_agreements and questions.thread_id, with the schema and every_row unchanged.","summary":"No test reaches the refusal of a home that holds a main mark above 38 but lacks questions.thread_id","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:36:04.779591Z","id":"dee22befb8fbe5c7149ce76fe8789ce189e01ccb150823d51795fff8b23ac696","body":{"detail":"app_numbered_from_41 builds MIGRATIONS[..APP_MIGRATION - 1 + app], and with_a_main_41 inserts its simulated migration at APP_MIGRATION - 1; a_home_of_this_numbering_takes_a_later_main_migration_and_the_apps_renumbering starts from installed_at_43 adopted by Store::open, which also lands at the current numbering. When the branch takes main's next migration, APP_MIGRATION becomes 42, so all three build a home of the new numbering (app from 42) and the layout homes of this build are left in (app from 41, k = 2 of the then three main marks) is no longer built by any test. Only the 39-43 layout keeps a frozen fixture (INSTALLED_AT_43). The rule itself is generic in k, so this is a coverage gap rather than a defect today, but it is the layout the owner's devices will hold after this build ships.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":4905},"end":{"line":4921},"content_hash":"1439a9bfe251410fd44241f678eafe17aaebdf8ff5036ae50482ba27630aa0b1"},"suggested_fix":"Build layouts by k rather than by APP_MIGRATION: a helper that runs migrations 1 to 38, the first k of main's above 38, then the first `app` of the app's (from a frozen copy of the app's SQL, as INSTALLED_AT_43 is), and a test that adopts every k from 0 to MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38.len() - 1 under NUMBERING through Store::open.","summary":"The tests of this build's own layout (the app's at 41 to 45) derive it from APP_MIGRATION, so they stop testing it once main adds a 41","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:36:04.779731Z","id":"32cf32c47d632afe47e2486dba5c10974f957740e853be12de28a57ce893d6e1","body":{"detail":"has_mark knows a table, or a column of artifacts only; the_app_migrations_follow_mains_in_this_order asserts every main mark above 38 is a CREATE TABLE. Main's own 38 added only columns (questions.thread_id and the sessions' engagement columns), which is why adoption checks it with has_column directly. A main migration above 40 that adds a column to another table, an index or a trigger needs has_mark extended; one that only changes rows (an UPDATE, a backfill) leaves nothing in the schema, so a home cannot be told to lack it and the leading-run rule cannot place the app's block. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md lines 1026-1035 promise 'one mark per new main migration and nothing else'. The test fails loudly for a non-table mark, so nothing breaks silently; the cost is that the next renumbering may need adoption code, not only a mark.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1457},"end":{"line":1465},"content_hash":"3dab28e28ef27c0c48cac6a408dcf9a0337c98b34c59d7358ce90cba7d8e28a0"},"suggested_fix":"Let a mark be (kind, table, name) for any table's column, an index or a trigger, and say in section 10.2 what a data-only main migration requires (for example a marker row, or landing the app's migrations on main first).","summary":"A main migration that adds no table cannot be given a mark, so 'a later renumbering adds one mark per new main migration and nothing else' (spec section 10.2) does not hold for it","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T03:36:04.779774Z","id":"4856bb2b04437321c63542cfb3933bd884b40158d8448045c4b946a620668e2a","body":{"detail":"RealDisk::sync_file and sync_dir call File::sync_all, which on Apple platforms is fcntl(F_FULLFSYNC) with no fallback; before_migrate_on (lines 108-112) turns any error into MigrationFailed, so the store does not open. SMB, AFP and some exFAT volumes answer F_FULLFSYNC with ENOTSUP, and some FUSE and network file systems answer fsync of a directory with EINVAL; a CLAX_HOME there opened fine before 219733273 and is refused on every launch after it, until migrated by another build. SQLite, with its fullfsync pragma, falls back to fsync when F_FULLFSYNC fails. The backups/ directory is also made by create_dir_all at line 96 without syncing its parent, so the first copy in a home can lose its directory entry on a power loss. Checked on APFS: copies of the owner's two Mac homes adopted from 43 to 45 with the syncs succeeding.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":53},"end":{"line":76},"content_hash":"84052ec85fcd5fab9036e006e97b0f3da5f3a397afd50b940648d90dc2b7b4c7"},"suggested_fix":"Fall back to fsync when F_FULLFSYNC fails, treat EINVAL or ENOTSUP from a directory sync as done (as SQLite and most databases do), and sync the home's root after creating backups/.","summary":"On a file system without F_FULLFSYNC, or one that refuses fsync of a directory, every open that would migrate is now refused","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:47.624281Z","id":"88d4b1bed281bd198582420d0d17562a3b5d5d982409c2ebfbd24284a13f1a25","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:633b10ec2","summary":"Fixed: before_migrate_on syncs through sync_file and sync_dir (crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs), which fall back from Flush::Full (F_FULLFSYNC on Apple platforms) to Flush::Plain (fsync) when the error is ENOTSUP, EOPNOTSUPP, EINVAL, ENOSYS or ErrorKind::Unsupported; a directory neither can sync is left to the file system; a real I/O error, or a file fsync cannot sync either, still refuses the open. A newly made backups/ has the home synced before the copy. Through the Disk seam: without_a_full_sync_the_copy_is_synced_with_fsync, a_directory_that_cannot_be_synced_is_left_to_its_file_system, a_real_io_error_refuses_the_open, and the_copy_is_synced_then_renamed_then_its_directory_synced (which now expects 'sync_dir full ax' first for a new backups/ and not for an existing one). Before the change four failed with 'Operation not supported (os error 45)' or an unwanted Ok, and the order test lacked the home's sync; at c25cb0469 all pass under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all, and bazelisk build --config=clippy //crates/clax-store:all is clean. Not exercised here: an actual SMB, AFP, exFAT or FUSE volume","supersedes":"4856bb2b04437321c63542cfb3933bd884b40158d8448045c4b946a620668e2a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:47.678425Z","id":"a28b19fcebfd792d6795e5c6014200d9bea1188885f0066e421c46c1d0c15fd8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:79d16aef3","summary":"Fixed: a_home_holding_a_main_mark_above_38_without_questions_thread_id_is_refused builds the app's layout from 38 (app_numbered_from_38, 5), runs main's 39 on it (legal_agreements) with the change left in the WAL, and asserts Store::open's MigrationFailed at 42 naming legal_agreements and 'lacks questions.thread_id', with user_version, schema and every row unchanged. With that refusal disabled in adopt_earlier_flutter_app the test failed ('table legal_agreements already exists ... a copy of the database as it was before is at ...'); restored, it passes under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all","supersedes":"2d8d421ad894d6ef2322b8487b230605c1f67d092f81e1d3b818154d79eacd5e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:47.731757Z","id":"3b2714256bc30d090f09e4ff85b879faff250f2a16cd0f8d7f1fa163889dd606","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:93c07fcf8","summary":"Fixed: crates/clax-store/tests/fixtures/old-migrations/flutter-app-4479a586c.sql freezes the app's five migrations as this numbering has them (41 to 45); app_after_main(home, k, app) builds migrations 1 to 38 + k, then the first app of the frozen ones, and app_numbered_from_41 is its k = 2, so this build's layout no longer derives from APP_MIGRATION. the_frozen_app_migrations_are_this_numberings checks the copy against MIGRATIONS from APP_MIGRATION; the_app_after_every_k_of_mains_migrations_opens_under_this_numbering opens every k from 0 to MAIN_MARKS_ABOVE_38.len() and every app prefix through Store::open under NUMBERING: adopted below that number, a copy at the old version first, the final schema, every row kept. With adoption made to skip k = 1 it failed (left None, right Some((40, 41))); restored, it passes under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all. When main adds a 41, k = 2 is one of the adopted ks of the same test","supersedes":"dee22befb8fbe5c7149ce76fe8789ce189e01ccb150823d51795fff8b23ac696","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:47.785230Z","id":"34861b874217ebee81e61c78fa7a5376ecda1ff88f59f1acfb8b0e4db973f87d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:1df922711","summary":"Fixed: marks are Mark values (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs): Table, Column(table, column) of any table, Index, or Row { table, predicate } for a data-only migration, which must leave such a row even on an empty database; has_mark checks each. assert_marks_made, called by the_app_migrations_follow_mains_in_this_order, checks every main mark above 38 from an empty database (absent before its migration, present after it and after every later one) instead of requiring CREATE TABLE. a_mark_is_a_table_a_column_of_any_table_an_index_or_a_row and a_later_main_migration_making_no_table_is_marked_and_adopted_around (simulated main 41s adding sessions.simulated_main_41, an index, and only rows with an install row as mark, adopted from k = 0, 1 and 2) failed while has_mark knew only tables and artifacts columns ('column sessions.simulated_main_41 after 41') and pass under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all; 56e90d987 keeps clippy clean. docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 10.2 says what a mark may be and what a data-only migration must leave","supersedes":"32cf32c47d632afe47e2486dba5c10974f957740e853be12de28a57ce893d6e1","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:34:47.837629Z","id":"bfbfa05ae6fea5765ff61b7c3c41df1fe3591c18784f669435b19c8ff1a35130","body":{"detail":"This covers the Mac homes only. The phone's home and the open through the embedded core (crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs with a schema-43 home dump) remain unchecked, so this concern stays open.","kind":"comment","references":"a658f3eb1f2c8a93d9fca1cf0fbbfaf5c116c73c28baac0d8761da3456dfe27f","summary":"Re-checked on copies of the owner's two Mac homes (the sandboxed container's and Application Support's clax-home): both copied and adopted from 43 to 45; the sorted content of all 68 pre-existing tables hashed the same before and after; PRAGMA integrity_check and foreign_key_check clean; all 25 versions and their 361 files served with sha256 matching the stored files; the originals' SHA-1s unchanged by the run","tags":["review","migrations","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:13.755774Z","id":"1118e379da5e0c1eb00835dd8a31d1e9cccb7c60823f899c59463f7ee196eb5e","body":{"detail":"Flush::Full goes through File::sync_all, which std retries on EINTR. Flush::Plain calls nix::unistd::fsync (nix 0.31), which returns Errno::EINTR as is; unsupported() (lines 186-210) does not list EINTR, so sync_file and sync_dir (lines 157-184) return it and before_migrate_on turns it into MigrationFailed. This path runs only where F_FULLFSYNC is unsupported (SMB, AFP, exFAT, FUSE), where fsync is slowest and a signal (SIGCHLD in the daemon, a terminal resize) is likeliest to land. The open is refused, not corrupted, and the next launch retries, but the documented rule is that only a real I/O error refuses it. No test covers EINTR.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":72},"end":{"line":81},"content_hash":"affaa3489521d08b737cc04f91480cee5a07b82c102c9c4ee2b4b786fefceeca"},"suggested_fix":"Retry Flush::Plain while it returns EINTR (loop on nix::unistd::fsync, as std's cvt_r does), and add an EINTR-then-Ok case to the Recording tests.","summary":"The fsync fallback (Flush::Plain) does not retry EINTR, so a signal during it refuses the open as if it were an I/O error","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:13.756076Z","id":"b7f054bc3935b3433a7fb2f8244b30a08f0722a7967ae214e8777884b5ed8160","body":{"detail":"before_migrate_on syncs home.root() only when dir.is_dir() is false. If that sync fails (a_real_io_error_refuses_the_open's first case, sync_dir full ax failing with EIO) or the process dies between create_dir_all and the sync, backups/ stays in place unsynced; every later open finds it a directory and skips the home's sync, so the copies made in it, though each synced with its directory, hang off an entry in the home that no sync has pushed to stable storage. the_copy_is_synced_then_renamed_then_its_directory_synced asserts this skip. Homes whose backups/ was made before 633b10ec2 are in the same state. The exposure needs a power loss soon after, and a bad migration besides, to cost data; the fix costs one directory sync per migration, which is rare.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"8f470aa8d17cf35b20db1e7150f86b87b189be2e99c8d501d29661038ba05650"},"suggested_fix":"Sync home.root() on every copy (after create_dir_all, whether or not it made the directory), and change the order test to expect 'sync_dir full ax' on the second copy too.","summary":"The home is synced only by the open that makes backups/, so a backups/ whose making was not followed by a successful home sync is never synced into the home","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T04:38:13.756646Z","id":"85188f394e03dd521b48e41fb16c9c05a878554cb54424325f39b99e4cdcb3eb","body":{"detail":"The doc on Mark (and spec section 10.2 in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md) requires a mark to stay present after every later migration, which assert_marks_made checks; nothing says it must survive the running store. Tables, columns and indexes do, but the store deletes rows: approvals.rs:948 deletes install rows by key (set_overflow), and backfill.rs:3035 deletes install's 'backfill' row. A Row mark on a row runtime code or the person can delete (a key another path clears, or any row of a user table) would, once gone, make adopt_earlier_flutter_app refuse a valid home ('holds the X but lacks the row of install where ...') when a later main mark is present, or rerun the data-only migration when it is the last. No migration uses a Row mark yet.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1302},"end":{"line":1329},"content_hash":"bbc9bb2e0328f777d9bd81ec069998e441f2d23331f6e34cf582a6f0b6c6ba5f"},"suggested_fix":"Add to Mark's doc and section 10.2 that a Row mark's row is never written or deleted outside its migration (for install, a key reserved to it, for example 'migration:<n>'), or confine Row marks to a fixed key pattern in install that has_mark builds itself.","summary":"Mark's contract binds a mark only through later migrations, so a Row mark whose row the store or the person removes at runtime breaks adoption","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:03:31.367308Z","id":"2a04653d49ff1c8cc026f9e1fd645b1d48389e62bef75538ebf33cdcbda442c9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:04dffaf72","summary":"Fixed: sync_file and sync_dir (crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs) make each sync, Flush::Full and the fsync fallback Flush::Plain, through uninterrupted(), which repeats it while it returns ErrorKind::Interrupted (EINTR), as File::sync_all does. backup::tests::a_sync_a_signal_interrupts_is_made_again (Recording failing sync_dir full ax, sync_file plain tmp twice and sync_dir plain backups with EINTR, each once per entry) failed before the change with MigrationFailed 'Interrupted system call (os error 4)' and passes after it under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all (696 passed)","supersedes":"1118e379da5e0c1eb00835dd8a31d1e9cccb7c60823f899c59463f7ee196eb5e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:03:32.195571Z","id":"b45fd0ab8b7ddae3b9f6a1a8019345af814ae89dd20ca9d411024359824be7e7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:0fc5dd08a","summary":"Fixed: before_migrate_on (crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs) runs create_dir_all and syncs home.root() before every copy, whether or not it made backups/. the_copy_is_synced_then_renamed_then_its_directory_synced now expects 'sync_dir full ax' on the second copy too, and a_backups_directory_whose_home_sync_failed_is_synced_by_the_next_copy (a first open whose home sync fails with EIO after making backups/, then a second open) expects the second open to sync the home first and refuse before any copy when that sync fails; both failed before the change and pass after it under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all (696 passed). efb31e7e1 formats the new test","supersedes":"b7f054bc3935b3433a7fb2f8244b30a08f0722a7967ae214e8777884b5ed8160","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:03:32.914495Z","id":"b1040764fdf0a4b057bcaf4e6fba7d6365aeefd7dc0eadb18dbda4b215353f73","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:982115b3a","summary":"Fixed: Mark::Row is gone; a data-only migration is marked by Mark::Marker(name) (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs). Its SQL starts with migration_marker!(name), which makes migration_marks (name TEXT PRIMARY KEY) with CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS (no migration or number of its own), triggers that RAISE(ABORT) on UPDATE and DELETE of it, and inserts the name; has_mark checks the table and the name. Mark's doc and docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-19-in-process-core-design.md section 10.2 require a mark to stay for as long as the database, whatever the running store or the person does. a_mark_is_a_table_a_column_of_any_table_an_index_or_a_marker, a_marker_is_never_changed_or_removed (DELETE and UPDATE of migration_marks refused, the marker still held) and a_later_main_migration_making_no_table_is_marked_and_adopted_around (the simulated data-only 41 now marked by Marker(simulated_main_41), adopted from k = 0, 1 and 2) pass under bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:all (696 passed); bazelisk build --config=clippy //crates/clax-store:all is clean","supersedes":"85188f394e03dd521b48e41fb16c9c05a878554cb54424325f39b99e4cdcb3eb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:10.949591Z","id":"0a60981378017b3bbe47a6d2a2033de2ab33a20a29a0afef5db96dc52506ace1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:db4a95dc9","summary":"record_push leaves out a pushed icon.svg the commit changes that fails icon::problem and the note says 'icon.svg was not taken (it breaks the icon rules: <rule>; still in git).'; an unchanged one is kept. The Page contract now says a push leaves it out. pushes::a_pushed_icon_that_breaks_the_icon_rules_is_left_out_and_named_in_the_note failed before (files held icon.svg) and passes in //crates/clax-content-git:integration.","supersedes":"9b65e346657055319a99ad7efe7c9f8d1df88b8f7580d250a03b92c3a7493e67","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:35:11.334689Z","id":"db8c145e939cc3dde0c1f34c70dc25f6b7535fa1fbc515dd2253c9918e3de5c5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:b6701cb90","summary":"artifacts::tests::restore_and_fork_carry_an_icon_the_rules_now_refuse_unchanged pins both (it fails with InvalidIcon(Element(\"script\")) when restore_version_async checks the icon), and docs/contract.md's restore and fork paragraphs say their files are copied without a publish's checks. //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test passes.","supersedes":"2e0e9213c3e288f487326f9506ddfbc1d5e2f6d4646573f0ab3b7be9b1a2fdee","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:40:59.465897Z","id":"77cd6afa09c12ad26da008eea1ba7cef6612fb3703e61c4a668aced72eee9326","body":{"detail":"Failure: once a job row names an artifact (a change) or a job_threads row names a thread, purging that artifact (crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs, the purge loop ending in \"DELETE FROM artifacts WHERE id = ?1\", around line 699), deleting a never-published draft (drafts.rs:262, 337), a fork's source (forks.rs:635), or deleting the thread (threads.rs:1767) fails with a FOREIGN KEY constraint error, since foreign_keys is ON (exec.rs:266) and those deletes list every dependent table but job_threads and jobs. No caller writes jobs yet (the routes come with the job routes), so nobody hits it today.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1284},"end":{"line":1315},"content_hash":"bfe2729df98e57f3066b52f0a40b6cf4bcef58abdd9dd055f22217979a8cd445"},"suggested_fix":"Have each hard delete clear the job tables it would orphan (DELETE FROM job_threads WHERE thread_id ...; UPDATE jobs SET artifact_id = NULL WHERE artifact_id = ...), or give the two columns ON DELETE CASCADE / SET NULL in this migration while it is unmerged; add a test that purges an artifact a job names.","summary":"jobs.artifact_id and job_threads.thread_id reference artifacts and threads with no ON DELETE, and the store's hard deletes do not clear them","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:40:59.466043Z","id":"d4ba1c8694af7acab90ac10f5af20b1a421a626c7ec2740940401990dbcd4221","body":{"detail":"Store::answer_job_question_tx (crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs) returns the job's row after the answer; close_question discards it and returns only the QuestionRow. The jobs topic (spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §8.1: Event::Job after every committed write of a job) then misses this write, and a worker waiting on the job hears of it only at its next full load.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":987},"end":{"line":989},"content_hash":"2ae8d9831b1b1218cdb65144ac17ca6f64d72855d065d3604238ae2b91cb55d7"},"suggested_fix":"Return the changed job (or its ID and rev) from close_question, or collect it in the store as inbox changes are collected, so the answer and decline routes publish Event::Job after the commit.","summary":"close_question moves a job back to running but drops the job's new row, so nothing can publish Event::Job for that change","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:40:59.466120Z","id":"0e88da634a1f5e615f65e729d62cc6c8b3ec70bcd97f51ed9d78c906492ae48f","body":{"detail":"Only an answer or a decline (Status::Answered, Status::Declined) reaches answer_job_question_tx; Close::Withdraw, Unwaited, Shutdown, Release and Expire leave the job_questions row unanswered and the job in waiting, which next(job) treats as 'nothing to do' (spec §7.4). Whether the app's questions can take those closes is not settled here.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":987},"end":{"line":989},"content_hash":"2ae8d9831b1b1218cdb65144ac17ca6f64d72855d065d3604238ae2b91cb55d7"},"summary":"A job waiting on a question that is withdrawn, released or expired stays waiting","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/backup.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:42:20.872335Z","id":"9ad8160eeafba4bb3cc26a266a9a2fd66dbbd47ea69686f518ac53fbcc790f80","body":{"detail":"88d5f406f reports Phase::BackingUp from Store::open_with (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs, the `if version != 0 && version < known` before backup::before_migrate) by re-deriving before_migrate_on's rule `version == 0 || version >= known` (this span). The two agree today; a change to either (a copy skipped for another reason, or made after an adoption renumbers user_version) makes the app's splash say 'backing up' with no copy, or copy without saying so.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":117},"end":{"line":120},"content_hash":"798345fa821ca1249ee86af772a217abdc83142172bcb144fc7c854fd68e5915"},"suggested_fix":"Pass the report to backup::before_migrate and have it report BackingUp itself just before VACUUM INTO, so the decision has one owner.","summary":"Whether a copy is made before migrating is decided twice: here, and restated in Store::open_with to report backing up","tags":["review","store","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.640485Z","id":"088975f545f5197703a766393776e3731f84af85d782b714eab8c149b985f325","body":{"detail":"Options weighed against spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §7.4 (the job rows are the one truth; the worker applies rows by rev) and §8.1:\n- SET NULL on jobs.artifact_id leaves a 'change' with no artifact, a row next(job) has no answer for, and leaves the person's request and comments (input_json, carry_json) behind after a purge whose point is to remove them.\n- A blocking delete (refuse with an error while a job names the artifact or thread) blocks purge forever, since done and cancelled jobs are never deleted, and the purge loop in artifacts.rs (around line 699) and the never-published draft deletes (artifacts.rs:609, drafts.rs:262 and 337) are not the person's to retry.\n- CASCADE matches the app's own earlier tables (migrations.rs:1218-1219, 1242, 1258, 1262 all use REFERENCES artifacts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE).\nCascade alone deletes rows without a rev bump, so a worker holding the job would never hear of it; the delete paths must move each open job they touch first.","kind":"comment","references":"77cd6afa09c12ad26da008eea1ba7cef6612fb3703e61c4a668aced72eee9326","span":{"start":{"line":1284},"end":{"line":1315},"content_hash":"bfe2729df98e57f3066b52f0a40b6cf4bcef58abdd9dd055f22217979a8cd445"},"suggested_fix":"In migration 46 (unmerged, edited in place): jobs.artifact_id REFERENCES artifacts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE; job_steps.job_id, job_threads.job_id, job_questions.job_id REFERENCES jobs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE; job_threads.thread_id REFERENCES threads(id) ON DELETE CASCADE; agent_read_consents.reader/source and draft_renders.draft_id REFERENCES artifacts(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, as db_read_grants does. Add jobs::artifact_going_tx(tx, aid) and jobs::thread_going_tx(tx, tid), called by soft delete, purge, the draft deletes and threads.rs:1767 before their DELETEs: each open job naming the artifact moves to cancelled with error_json {\"code\":\"artifact_deleted\"} and rev + 1; each job losing a job_threads row gets rev + 1. With the job change hook of d4ba1c86's reply, Event::Job follows. Tests: purge an artifact a done job and an open job name (purge succeeds, the open job's Event::Job says cancelled, no job rows remain); delete a thread a job answers (succeeds, the job's rev moves).","summary":"Proposed decision: ON DELETE CASCADE on every job-table foreign key, with the delete paths ending open jobs first; not SET NULL, not a blocking delete","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.640913Z","id":"f0b3b124d31d8b3a1f7773117d725e85c48d9fd2d0103a5538cc3239f3df151a","body":{"detail":"Returning the job from close_question fixes this caller only; the cascades proposed on 77cd6afa, the future publish and reply steps (Task 21) and any later write would each need the same care. crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs:349-362 already records inbox_items and approval_requests rowids in an update hook, drops them in the rollback hook, and with_tx (lib.rs:573-600) hands them to a listener after tx.commit(). A `jobs` branch there makes every committed job write, whichever path made it, reach Event::Job exactly once per transaction.","kind":"comment","references":"d4ba1c8694af7acab90ac10f5af20b1a421a626c7ec2740940401990dbcd4221","span":{"start":{"line":987},"end":{"line":989},"content_hash":"2ae8d9831b1b1218cdb65144ac17ca6f64d72855d065d3604238ae2b91cb55d7"},"suggested_fix":"Add job_changes: Arc<Mutex<Vec<i64>>> (rowids of jobs, deduplicated) to the update hook for table == \"jobs\", clear it in the rollback hook, take it in with_tx after commit, map rowid to (id, client, state, step, rev) and call a JobListener the router sets (Store::set_job_listener), which publishes Event::Job on the jobs topic. Test in jobs.rs: answer a question a job asked through close_question and assert the listener heard that job at its new rev; a rolled-back write is heard of not at all.","summary":"Fix by construction: record changed job rows with the write connection's update hook, as inbox_items and approval_requests are, and tell a job listener after the commit","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.641439Z","id":"758334a6f6aa7cdc689189cde865ab327850e48714f5b56c6cb92b1878129169","body":{"detail":"Release and Expire refuse an ask question (not_mirrored, questions.rs:938-940); Shutdown and Unwaited are reached only for hook questions (crates/clax-server/src/routes/questions.rs:476-477, crates/clax-http/src/views/question.rs:206); withdraw_hook_questions_on_start withdraws hook questions with a bare UPDATE (questions.rs:425-426, 1105) that bypasses close_question entirely. Withdraw is open to any session over POST /api/sessions/<sid>/questions/<qid>/withdraw (routes/questions.rs:525-539), so a waiting job's question can be withdrawn and the job then waits forever.","kind":"comment","references":"0e88da634a1f5e615f65e729d62cc6c8b3ec70bcd97f51ed9d78c906492ae48f","span":{"start":{"line":987},"end":{"line":989},"content_hash":"2ae8d9831b1b1218cdb65144ac17ca6f64d72855d065d3604238ae2b91cb55d7"},"suggested_fix":"Call answer_job_question_tx (renamed close_job_question_tx) for every terminal status, storing the outcome (answered with answers, declined, withdrawn; see the job_questions record on jobs.rs answer_job_question_tx) and moving the job from waiting to running, so next(job) answers the ask call with that outcome. ask_job_question refuses a question whose source is not 'ask' (invalid_question), so the bulk hook withdrawal never concerns a job. Test: ask, withdraw through close_question(Close::Withdraw), the job is running with outcome withdrawn.","summary":"For an app's ask question only Close::Withdraw is reachable; store every close's outcome in the job and refuse hook questions at ask_job_question","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.641977Z","id":"f6d7f7d1dbd2f05e35de9e10a13e9932eec055ea9e8079afe82b8344950964a9","body":{"detail":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-10-19-in-process-core.md Task 20 lists crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs (the installed home ends at 46); ls crates/clax-embed/tests shows embed.rs, ffi.rs, log.rs, nulls.c only. The store-level adoption to 46 is covered by migrations::tests::a_database_with_the_jobs_tables_at_another_version_is_adopted and the installed_at_43 path asserting user_version 46.","kind":"comment","references":"a658f3eb1f2c8a93d9fca1cf0fbbfaf5c116c73c28baac0d8761da3456dfe27f","span":{"start":{"line":1344},"end":{"line":1412},"content_hash":"acc84b98e364b941ad664dec80a3bae17afc465c95a36b2058c4eecf572dcd1b"},"summary":"Task 20's part of this is outstanding too: crates/clax-embed/tests/old_homes.rs does not exist, so nothing opens the installed schema-43 home through the core up to 46","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.642048Z","id":"aea075980cdfbab1c00d5fc35eb0ddd9a1c1a696726dbcdffa1dd9348abb92f9","body":{"detail":"job_questions has PRIMARY KEY (job_id, question_id), no UNIQUE (question_id) and no REFERENCES questions(id) (migrations.rs, migration 46). Two jobs asking one question is accepted by ask_job_question; answer_job_question_tx picks one with ORDER BY job_id LIMIT 1, and the other stays waiting forever. A question ID naming no question is accepted and waits forever. JobQuestion.answer is Option<String> where None is pending, Some(\"null\") a decline and any other text the answers' JSON: three outcomes in one stringly field, which a withdrawal (0e88da63) cannot join without a fourth spelling. Questions are never hard-deleted (no DELETE FROM questions in crates/clax-store/src), so the foreign key costs nothing.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":580},"end":{"line":612},"content_hash":"23547c65a901a041c9094c32312dd06d16dfab650f78954a77f7d5db2ce9020a"},"suggested_fix":"Migration 46 in place: job_questions (job_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES jobs(id) ON DELETE CASCADE, question_id TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE REFERENCES questions(id), outcome TEXT CHECK (outcome IN ('answered','declined','withdrawn')), answers_json TEXT, PRIMARY KEY (job_id, question_id), CHECK ((outcome = 'answered') = (answers_json IS NOT NULL))). In Rust, pub enum JobAnswer { Pending, Answered(serde_json::Value), Declined, Withdrawn } in JobQuestion. ask_job_question answers invalid_question for an unknown question or one another job asked. Spec §8.1's SQL changes with it. Tests: a second job asking the same question is refused; an unknown question ID is refused.","summary":"job_questions lets one question belong to many jobs and to no question at all, and keeps a decline as the JSON text 'null'; answer_job_question_tx then answers only the first job by ID","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.642103Z","id":"ccd00e63f86c024a4c7b0646e4fab9faaf160e431152be05e63896dc5b1bac22","body":{"detail":"The UPDATE sets state = 'waiting' with no condition, so a done or cancelled job is reopened to waiting, and a paused or stopped one is moved without the worker asking. The question's status is not read: spec §7.4's Ask effect creates the question and then PUTs it on the job, two calls; a worker killed between them that re-asks with the same question ID after the person answered, or an answer landing between the two calls, leaves job_questions unanswered (answer_job_question_tx found no row when the answer came) and the job in waiting, which next(job) treats as nothing to do.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":469},"end":{"line":491},"content_hash":"ffb47339f084bf3cba3281fe90d85408020a0cb421841466636bd9161f15be55"},"suggested_fix":"In the same transaction: refuse a job in cancelled or done (JobError::Moved with its row, or a job_closed refusal); read questions.status; when the question is already closed, store its outcome and leave the job's state as it is (bumping rev); move to waiting only from running. Tests: ask a question answered beforehand (the job stays running with the answer stored); ask on a done job (refused, row unchanged).","summary":"ask_job_question moves a job of any state to waiting, and a job asked about a question that is already closed waits forever","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.642148Z","id":"95e2323382e4c31c27355b3a5b54e7e41e07cb1dbab8a415d94cfc1d01fe534b","body":{"detail":"patch_job checks only that the state is one of STATES (jobs.rs:19-29, a copy of the SQL CHECK). It moves done or cancelled jobs back to running, moves a job to waiting with no unanswered question (nothing will ever move it out), and moves a waiting job to running while its question is unanswered (next(job) then re-asks, making a second question). commit_step (jobs.rs:500-527) commits steps on a cancelled or done job and with done = true turns cancelled into done. JobRow.state and JobPatch.state are String, so every reader matches on text (the tests compare state.as_str()). Spec §7.4's rule that the rows are the one truth holds only if the core refuses rows no sequence of legal moves reaches.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":370},"end":{"line":411},"content_hash":"0415343178fc1b834e942dabb7935a96265d14eb9b3959abca12947cb1f3a1f4"},"suggested_fix":"pub enum JobState { Queued, Running, Waiting, Paused, Stopped, Failed, Cancelled, Done } with serde rename_all lowercase and ToSql/FromSql, replacing STATES and the String fields. A fn may_move(from, to) table in jobs.rs: cancelled and done are final (every write refuses with JobError::Moved(row)); waiting is entered only by ask_job_question and left to running only by a question's close (patch to paused, stopped, failed or cancelled allowed); a patch to running of a job with an unanswered question lands in waiting. commit_step refuses a final job. Tests: each refused move leaves the row and rev unchanged; paused with an unanswered question resumes to waiting.","summary":"The store keeps no job state machine: patch_job and commit_step accept any move, including out of done and cancelled, and job states are strings","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.642192Z","id":"6958dd4bfc3aca046a4b50e9360d3f54a55332fddb9864b04751f3939c65d269","body":{"detail":"job_tx maps Ok(Err(Moved | Conflict | NotFound)) to a committed transaction. Every closure today refuses before it writes, so nothing goes wrong yet, but Task 21's commit_publish_step inserts the version and then applies document writes that can refuse with doc_moved; if that refusal is a JobError variant, the version commits without its step row, the exact 'did the publish land?' unknown spec §8.1 says cannot arise.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":278},"end":{"line":286},"content_hash":"37550b0bdd451fd6dd66f465b20be8a557a88aa0065f11da9bbb8894db3dab7a"},"suggested_fix":"Roll back on every Err: have job_tx run with_tx with a closure returning Err(CoreError) for any refusal while stashing the JobError in a local Option, then return the stashed error; or give Store a with_tx_result that rolls back on Err(E) for any E. Test: a closure that inserts a job_steps row and then returns JobError::Conflict leaves no row.","summary":"job_tx commits what its closure wrote before any refusal other than JobError::Store","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.642367Z","id":"93e744c464aad06a2570d9aad4ea76dcc70a0ca3e577cc983a85d7ad55b3efd2","body":{"detail":"jobs_tables_disagree reads pragma_table_info (name, type, notnull, default, pk). It does not see REFERENCES clauses, ON DELETE actions, CHECK constraints or indexes. Changing migration 46 in place as 77cd6afa's reply proposes (ON DELETE CASCADE, job_questions UNIQUE and outcome CHECK) makes this matter: a home whose jobs tables an earlier build of the migration made would pass adoption and keep the old foreign keys, so purges would fail there. The granularity (the jobs table as the one mark, the other six held to be all present or all absent) is right: the migration's seven CREATEs run in one transaction, and Mark has no multi-table form to need.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1610},"end":{"line":1659},"content_hash":"41f452286c45ed2919c1633a0d725df253c56b52649627f0a65de1dbfbe24ffa"},"suggested_fix":"Compare each table's sqlite_master.sql, and the jobs_open index's, with the in-memory copy made from jobs_sql (the stored text is the CREATE as written, so the same SQL gives the same text), instead of or beside pragma_table_info. Add a refusal case to a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused with job_threads recreated without ON DELETE CASCADE, and one with jobs_open dropped.","summary":"Adoption compares the jobs tables' columns only, so a table differing in a foreign key, a CHECK or the jobs_open index is adopted as migration 46's","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:47:07.642515Z","id":"06a22f77d3cf6102127e86c7b0edd4dbf5bbaf362b7a47af446b1b4da305c59f","body":{"detail":"job_threads.stopped and draft_renders.clean are INTEGER with no CHECK, rev has no lower bound, and input_json, plan_json, carry_json, error_json, result_json and summary_json take any text; read_job (jobs.rs:185-202) then fails the whole open_jobs read on one bad row, so one corrupt job hides every job from the worker. The SQL is spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §8.1's verbatim, so tightening it amends the spec.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1284},"end":{"line":1339},"content_hash":"5547590810f6d6b618fabe796127bdf2278cc198a0374531db6d8c2215b66c19"},"suggested_fix":"Add CHECK (stopped IN (0, 1)), CHECK (clean IN (0, 1)), CHECK (rev >= 1), and CHECK (json_valid(x)) on each _json column (x IS NULL OR json_valid(x) for the nullable ones), and amend §8.1's SQL to match. A store test inserting each bad value directly sees a CHECK constraint failure.","summary":"Migration 46's SQL lets values in that no job can have: booleans that are any integer, a rev of 0 or less, and JSON columns holding text that is not JSON","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:13.115218Z","id":"b387083e9373b68045139c7444c97452127068340d1d68d0356ffec3710dd738","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1154-1174, record f6358543.\n\nA push to Cloudflare Artifacts whose pushed event is lost, late or never delivered (no subscription, locally: the queue is simulated and receives none, crates/clax-worker/wrangler.jsonc queues) stays unrecorded until the next publish of the artifact, so viewers see the older version meanwhile. The prototype also reconciles lazily on reads, at most every RECONCILE_EVERY_MS (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts reconcileLazily). Fix: reconcile from the artifact read routes when main has moved past the current version's commit, rate-limited per artifact.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1335},"end":{"line":1355},"content_hash":"5aea8e38f17328396770571e0e3d99efadde21ae073543404d5fa024591c706c"},"summary":"Pushed commits are recorded on a push, an Artifacts event or a publish, but not when an artifact is read","supersedes":"6dbd24d8ca07de749b55acdb966d0f733668729ba077d8793a3208070c02dafe","tags":["status:deferred","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:13.396633Z","id":"57e2edf87941ebde7cbc7877e354fe47f4f39b29779dee9c3f6ccf28aaab6bd2","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1246-1268, record 8c8d734d.\n\nrecord_version_locked calls revoke_blind_tokens with the publisher for VersionStep::Write when expected > 0, which is ContentStore::repo_tokens (DoLedger: POST token/live to RepoDO) even when no token is held. That is one subrequest on every publish's path (time to usable), plus a Visibility per agent token. Skipping needs to know no agent token is live without asking RepoDO, for example a held-token count the instance keeps from mint and revoke answers.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1426},"end":{"line":1448},"content_hash":"6ed8171b4db41878a2abb7fa629ab98219240d7b92eab16c5ff30da26880ff29"},"summary":"Every publish of an existing artifact asks the push ledger for the repository's tokens before its commit: on the Worker one RepoDO call per publish","supersedes":"b3ddffd255fec19e18df53ad65cf1e950d390c7ae90d58dd8a2a17e1c9e1a351","tags":["perf","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:13.886305Z","id":"875009059bbe0f4b089bf2f76592580189ea77b1d551d43cd2319feebf267121","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1284-1293, record bd81b2ff.\n\nArtifactLocks (content/mod.rs) serialise version writes within one process, so there the loser waits and then sees Conflict (concurrent_publishes_with_same_if_version_yield_one_winner). Across processes the loser's content write fails first; it is mapped to Conflict only when the artifact has already moved past the expected version. Nothing is corrupted (the loser removes nothing it did not write). The daemon is the only writer of versions today.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1464},"end":{"line":1473},"content_hash":"4904f3490dcc2f9f92baa1aaa49032071480c9eaf3740604defd236f4657e508"},"summary":"Two processes publishing the same version at once: the loser gets the content store's AlreadyExists error, not Conflict, while the winner has not yet recorded it","supersedes":"df2d0cb05a2220e63b4c9b7580be5a967e85a24c8367324213a738e89b82e06d","tags":["content-store","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.027775Z","id":"c31f1a6782d78e719fed9cabcd8c400b7774002ff392f8eaed122f75aa4560ed","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/artifacts.rs:1415-1432, record 7e511288.\n\nStore::version_meta resolves p.person, else the session's person, else the owner, before the content write; version_authors (artifacts.rs:817) resolves the row's person again inside the transaction. They agree today (tests a_version_write_names_its_publisher_agent_and_note), but a change to one rule that misses the other makes git's Clax-Publisher disagree with the row.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:9f99ad872417faa2c56a8038f471dc5e83cf3124","span":{"start":{"line":1603},"end":{"line":1620},"content_hash":"48d111421f495d2e72c03035f37a629a7bd29de6662dec8fbd17c5f02aa85418"},"suggested_fix":"Resolve the person once before the content lock and pass it to version_authors.","summary":"The publisher the content store is told and the one the version row records are resolved by separate code","supersedes":"98301473f1f373e458193db70f6a438e1b18328b2aee02d82f711e3b7a2b5cc0","tags":["review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.104120Z","id":"f5c9854666f430a55d9af6e288c762f3b35668c9bb91adfd23ec55c3fc0d2b65","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs:144-152, record d3d39306.\n\nA refused commit stays on main (it is neither recorded nor tagged), and the stand-in refuses non-fast-forward pushes (clax-git ServeOptions deny_non_fast_forwards), so the only way past it is a push over it by someone who may publish. That commit is recorded with every file changed since the newest version authored by its pusher (record_push), so a refused or revoked person's changes reach other people's agents as, say, the owner's under the visibility filter; its note names the refused commits. The hosted prototype credits a changed blob to every author it already had in history (hosted/src/do/artifact.ts recordPushes, blobAuthors); here a refused commit's blobs have no recorded author. Fix: credit paths whose blob equals one in a refused commit to that commit's pusher as well, or refuse the commit over it until those paths match the newest version.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:ceb68d89ddb1093063205296d2bc440d12630f5a","span":{"start":{"line":148},"end":{"line":156},"content_hash":"8c34d7356614154fc05784b37020214d4aab0dc8a7a3271396030174350c9b1e"},"summary":"A commit recorded over refused commits carries their changes as its own pusher's words","supersedes":"21408fbc3461f529c576398df20037d37e37302cd720d40e4993a919f8b29fc3","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.188113Z","id":"0f64c393d517f09b00d65f8ff4cd634eb7e287fa8cc4976754fc8691a37d3d20","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-core/src/store/pushes.rs:475-487, record 6d8f2fc3.\n\nPushes to Artifacts' own git endpoint never pass RepoDO, so RepoDO's ledger has no git_pushes row for their commits (crates/clax-worker/src/repos/db.rs record_push, written only by tokens::note_push from RepoDO's /git/ route), and the queue consumer reconciles with Pusher::default() (crates/clax-worker/src/lib.rs queue). pushers_of then gives every such commit the fallback, the owner: the owner becomes the version's publisher and the author of its changed files, and Store::standing allows it, whoever held the Artifacts token. clax_git::events::event_repo reads only the repository's name; the event's documented payload (ref, before, after, commits; crates/clax-git/src/events.rs:21-25) names no token or actor that is known here. Fix: once the pushed event's schema names the token (Artifacts tokens are entered in git_tokens with hash NULL by tokens::mint) or the actor, have the queue consumer enter a git_pushes row for the event's after commit with that token's holder before it asks the instance to reconcile.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:ceb68d89ddb1093063205296d2bc440d12630f5a","span":{"start":{"line":488},"end":{"line":500},"content_hash":"38cc39ea7d33382de52e273c944e0c51a787210b5289531ea9b52b303e7a18bd"},"summary":"A push straight to Cloudflare Artifacts is credited to the owner and passes the rights recheck as the owner","supersedes":"f3f7661c5d334f6586ee72deeba5ba75b02ba0e8319faa6dfcb469e017472491","tags":["security","revisit:Cloudflare Artifacts' pushed-event schema is known","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.296942Z","id":"fdf948196609a3711080389453e81500cbfc1dab8bad21a7a0dd660fa59175e5","body":{"detail":"The content store's VersionWrite carries files only from the version before (crates/clax-core/src/content/mod.rs), so restore_version_async reads version n's bytes and puts them; the audit record still names only unchanged files as carried (VersionStep::Restore). An artifact with large files costs their whole size per restore; a carry-from-version in ContentStore would avoid it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1142},"end":{"line":1251},"content_hash":"d24c354e8db190a006d8615bbd7df669c5326b66d2eb1d33addab40d68176909"},"summary":"A restore reads every file of the restored version into memory and writes them all again as the new version's puts","supersedes":"89ea1abf01b86c95266b5c54ebac8e7fb9734be7e8fd1f514c36d3382112b44f","tags":["restore","content","rebase","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.545853Z","id":"f755decc0b6ac409da8c69ab1fc195ac0d901f09ba7dc7c878e52691c355776d","body":{"detail":"pushed_files compares a commit's tree with the version's tagged commit (crates/clax-content-git/src/lib.rs pushed_files), and that commit holds the refused icon.svg, so the next push that leaves the file alone reports PushedContent::Same for a path the version below lacks. record_push sends that to skipped (line 365, \"Left out of the version below as well\"), and push_note's generic sentence names it as over the path or size limits or not a regular file. Inputs: push icon.svg containing <script>, then push any commit that changes only index.html; the second version's note says \"1 file was not taken (over Clax's path or size limits, or not a regular file; still in git): icon.svg.\" The test a_pushed_icon_that_breaks_the_icon_rules_is_left_out_and_named_in_the_note (crates/clax-content-git/tests/pushes.rs) changes icon.svg on each push after the bad one, so it never reaches this case.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":363},"end":{"line":367},"content_hash":"ea0b1a74f881a2c41654f2edf6c8be6f24803d4a4e84444ffb4f876b0eb21292"},"suggested_fix":"For a Same icon.svg the version below lacks, run clax_core::icon::problem on the bytes (or remember the rule) and name it as bad_icon is named; extend the pushes test with a push after the bad one that leaves icon.svg unchanged.","summary":"After a push leaves a bad icon.svg out, every later push that does not change it names icon.svg among files \"over Clax's path or size limits, or not a regular file\", not the icon rule","tags":["review","pushes","icons","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T05:49:14.546402Z","id":"b8858462098038eded8111fbbe059e6fd729d3cd588d17e4f7d1ee4874d4eb0a","body":{"detail":"Versions keep files, label and note but not the title, description, icon and capabilities in force (crates/clax-core/src/model.rs Version; the versions table). So restore_version_declaring_async takes the declaration from the caller: the Clax app's updater keeps it in SnapshotMeta (apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/doc_snapshot.dart) and passes it back (updater.dart _rollBackVersion), while the other roll-backs restore files only and keep whatever declaration the failed version set: finish.dart _undo (api.restoreVersion(aid, base, ifVersion: landed)), loop.dart _restore, app_screen.dart's Restore and home_recovery.dart. Two concepts share one call: \"put version n back\" (history, unchecked) and \"set a declaration\" (a publish's checks). If each version recorded its declaration, versions:restore would restore n's files and declaration together with no client-supplied fields (label and note aside), RestoreDeclaration's title, icon and capabilities would go, and the app's roll-backs would agree. The cost is a migration adding the columns, with NULL (keep the current declaration) for versions written before it.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":1160},"end":{"line":1175},"content_hash":"e61da67757d75a2c169eaaa4adab109c8ee114feacb66470b159fdfc6f6ee44c"},"summary":"Restore with a declaration is history plus a client's memory of history: recording each version's declaration in the core would let versions:restore put version n back whole, and every roll-back would mean the same","tags":["review","api","restore","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:22:06.173900Z","id":"8fdf0bf6ac63c1123ebef9c8f2ab57d6b0d7846437862f562724e8e03e17216b","body":{"detail":"Not taken: it adds columns to the versions table (crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs), which main shares, with NULL (keep the current declaration) for versions written before it. Instead each client roll-back captures its base's Declaration before the change and passes it to versions:restore (apps/clax_app/lib/clax/api.dart RollBack.rollBack; apps/clax_app/lib/agent/tools/finish.dart _undo; apps/clax_app/lib/agent/loop.dart _restore and the single-call undo; apps/clax_app/lib/bundle/updater.dart _rollBackVersion), and the person's restores of an older version keep the current declaration. Limits of the client capture: a change made by another client is undone only by that client; a restore cannot clear an icon word (COALESCE in the store), so a roll-back to a base with none keeps the current one; a ledger record written before Declaration was kept restores files only.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":1171},"end":{"line":1255},"content_hash":"5b68a9f323bb759d823fa868f0d41cbe6ca1bf1046eb8e9f4af897307d252342"},"summary":"Per-version declarations in the core: each version records the title, description, icon and capabilities in force, and versions:restore puts version n back whole with no client-supplied declaration","tags":["restore","api","revisit:the versions table next takes a migration on main, or a roll-back by another client must restore the declaration, or the Versions tab must restore an older version's declaration","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:22:06.175456Z","id":"27011e4619269bc20f7cd92a0c3364103dea3b47b9893a3bd6dfaba70fb5c07d","body":{"detail":"Done in c78ef5537: finish's undo, the single-call loop's undo and recovery's undo (from the ledger record's Declaration) restore the base's title, icon and capabilities with its files; the updater already did (c550b615d). The person's restores keep the current declaration. Per-version declarations in the core are recorded as an alternative on restore_version_declaring_async.","kind":"comment","references":"b8858462098038eded8111fbbe059e6fd729d3cd588d17e4f7d1ee4874d4eb0a","summary":"Owner's decision (2026-10-19): keep versions:restore with a client-supplied declaration, and fix the bug it exposed: every roll-back of a failed change puts its base's declaration back, not only the updater's","tags":["restore","status:decided","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/artifacts.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:22:06.176570Z","id":"1e4573632505ca0f889ca85dac0bbec506a6a57e0af7533fa573a08ecaa4d2a9","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:c78ef5537","summary":"Decided by the owner (2026-10-19, the status:decided reply on this thread): versions:restore keeps its client-supplied declaration, and every roll-back of a failed change now restores its base's declaration (c78ef5537; finish_test, loop_single_call_test, worker_test and ledger_test roll-back tests pass under Bazel). Per-version declarations in the core stay an alternative with a revisit tag on restore_version_declaring_async.","supersedes":"b8858462098038eded8111fbbe059e6fd729d3cd588d17e4f7d1ee4874d4eb0a","tags":["reason:wontfix","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/pushes.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:26:11.414217Z","id":"f46629916190f83539a147d0ef486022f09d5ccd8dc3fc2208a7c8337723e709","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:bf6ba4c1d","summary":"Fixed: ContentStore::pushed_files compares a pushed commit with the base version's published files, so a path its tagged commit holds but the version left out is read again and record_push runs the icon rule on it. crates/clax-content-git/tests/pushes.rs a_pushed_icon_that_breaks_the_icon_rules_is_left_out_and_named_in_the_note now pushes once more with icon.svg unchanged: it failed with \"1 file was not taken (over Clax's path or size limits...): icon.svg. Four\" and passes now (//crates/clax-content-git:integration).","supersedes":"f755decc0b6ac409da8c69ab1fc195ac0d901f09ba7dc7c878e52691c355776d","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
