{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.532474Z","id":"4e74a328ee923bbbcd62cda9dc147eca8bc724fbb94f7ce49d283e873fdde090","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:2c4b4f468","summary":"job_tx rolls back on every error and answers the refusal as the closure gave it; jobs::tests::a_refusal_after_a_write_rolls_the_write_back (a job_steps insert, then JobError::Conflict, leaves no row; a Moved refusal after an UPDATE leaves the row as it was) failed before the change and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"6958dd4bfc3aca046a4b50e9360d3f54a55332fddb9864b04751f3939c65d269","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.639790Z","id":"c6bf71d6ee0032cd7c6cb9c15969745c308597adb268c8c817571525a0103fe7","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:fac3581a3","summary":"JobState enum (ToSql/FromSql, serde lowercase) replaces STATES and the String fields; jobs::may_move is the one table, obeyed by patch_job, set_job_thread, remove_job_thread, ask_job_question, commit_step and the close of a job's question; spec §8.1 gains the table. jobs::tests::done_and_cancelled_jobs_refuse_every_write, a_patch_never_moves_a_job_to_queued_waiting_or_done, only_a_running_job_that_asks_moves_to_waiting and a_job_resumed_while_its_question_is_open_waits each failed against the old moves and pass. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"95e2323382e4c31c27355b3a5b54e7e41e07cb1dbab8a415d94cfc1d01fe534b","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.757806Z","id":"391a42ec1b975a6f74eb312a960cd57e27c0b9c7ecea67b42850617e2864054b","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:d71e1fa89","summary":"Migration 46 in place: job_questions.question_id UNIQUE REFERENCES questions(id), outcome CHECKed to answered/declined/withdrawn with answers_json present exactly for an answer; JobQuestion.answer is JobAnswer {Pending, Answered, Declined, Withdrawn}; ask_job_question answers invalid_question for an unknown question or another job's. jobs::tests::a_question_belongs_to_one_job_and_must_exist failed before and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"aea075980cdfbab1c00d5fc35eb0ddd9a1c1a696726dbcdffa1dd9348abb92f9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.816521Z","id":"8ee612dd1d43a8a8be2b66a52e9ed0ab0bd59c2a21abdfe2ab61f2dc321190a3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:035a4031c","summary":"close_question stores every ending close (answered, declined, withdrawn) through close_job_question_tx and moves the job by may_move; ask_job_question refuses a hook question (invalid_question). jobs::tests::a_withdrawn_question_moves_the_job_back_with_its_outcome and a_job_asks_only_the_ask_tools_questions failed before and pass. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"0e88da634a1f5e615f65e729d62cc6c8b3ec70bcd97f51ed9d78c906492ae48f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:58.874547Z","id":"4c771de967a0e0180c9da78d25b41c7da1bd74babf3db0294309d493ae9a907e","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:653b45e0a","summary":"ask_job_question refuses a final job (job_moved), reads the question's status in its transaction, stores a closed question's outcome at once and keeps the job's state, and moves only a running job to waiting. jobs::tests::a_question_closed_before_it_is_recorded_is_stored_at_once failed before and passes; done_and_cancelled_jobs_refuse_every_write covers the done job. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"ccd00e63f86c024a4c7b0646e4fab9faaf160e431152be05e63896dc5b1bac22","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.215273Z","id":"3b9c60109aa1809ae65647458222d9c32fe28755062cd368d0bbcb2e6067e180","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:3628d65a5","summary":"The write connection's update hook records every written jobs rowid (crates/clax-store/src/lib.rs, beside inbox_items and approval_requests); with_tx reads them before the commit and Store::set_job_listener's listener hears each changed job once after it, never on a rollback. Event::Job itself is Task 21's: its router installs the listener and publishes. jobs::tests::every_committed_job_change_is_heard_once_whatever_made_it (create, patch, ask, then an answer through close_question heard at its new rev, and a rolled-back write unheard) failed without the hook branch and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"d4ba1c8694af7acab90ac10f5af20b1a421a626c7ec2740940401990dbcd4221","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.498730Z","id":"86dbfee51d67bc500f286ff713642134a507d9ead5a50b2d94fe5618861dd446","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e834cba53","summary":"Migration 46 in place: every job-table foreign key, agent_read_consents.reader/source and draft_renders.draft_id ON DELETE CASCADE, with indexes on the child columns; artifact_going_tx (soft delete, purge, zero-version delete, both draft deletes) cancels open jobs with error artifact_deleted and rev + 1, thread_going_tx and artifact_threads_going_tx (thread delete, purge) forget the thread with rev + 1. jobs::tests::a_deleted_artifact_cancels_its_open_jobs_and_a_purge_takes_them, deleting_a_thread_a_job_answers_moves_the_job and deleting_a_draft_or_an_empty_artifact_takes_its_jobs_and_consents failed (FOREIGN KEY constraint failed, or the job left queued) and pass. forks.rs:635 is a test's own DELETE, not a delete path. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"77cd6afa09c12ad26da008eea1ba7cef6612fb3703e61c4a668aced72eee9326","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.715124Z","id":"337847aac11b5e3e28cca5b66eb61332802d749b6ff0de84aac21f35b0f6e24d","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:dac8adf4e","summary":"Migration 46 in place and spec §8.1: CHECK (stopped IN (0, 1)), CHECK (clean IN (0, 1)), CHECK (rev >= 1) and json_valid on every _json column (NULL passes where allowed). jobs::tests::the_schema_refuses_values_no_job_can_have failed before and passes. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"06a22f77d3cf6102127e86c7b0edd4dbf5bbaf362b7a47af446b1b4da305c59f","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.892100Z","id":"3753621335d201201c85481b3d8b0cf02dd99230c289ce1eaf9d1fc50d65fa92","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:775ca260d","summary":"jobs_tables_disagree compares each jobs table's and each of its indexes' sqlite_master SQL, normalised by normalised_sql (comments and spacing), with the in-memory copy, refusing a missing or extra index. migrations::tests::a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused gains job_threads without its cascades and jobs_open dropped (both failed before, pass), and sql_is_compared_without_its_comments_and_spacing tests the normaliser. bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test: PASSED (Bazel, at 87d1a1397)","supersedes":"93e744c464aad06a2570d9aad4ea76dcc70a0ca3e577cc983a85d7ad55b3efd2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.964306Z","id":"a750112f6d12a22d29bc78e73a1a127476ccc120bf00b895496c0f152b524f85","body":{"detail":"artifact_going_tx (jobs.rs:987-1024) and patch_job to cancelled (or failed, stopped) move the job but leave its unclosed job_questions question open: the person still sees and may answer a question no worker will read. The close is then stored nowhere (close_job_question_tx returns None for a final job). Withdrawing the job's open questions when it becomes final, in the same transaction (close_question's Close::Withdraw logic factored to run inside a caller's transaction), would end both together.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":987},"end":{"line":1024},"content_hash":"e220c0b4094b41b60e1b35a801dc66c1e69428dab2d99074b977606edc6752d5"},"summary":"Cancelling a job leaves the question it waits on open in the person's inbox","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:27:59.964533Z","id":"b5d2b6fa2bc784fc54b6c1b62bc9075235c75f6e23c5e0f75af8470325682359","body":{"detail":"Their foreign keys cascade only on a hard delete (a purge, a draft's delete). The soft delete, which is how artifacts are deleted, leaves them until a purge, unlike db_read_grants, net_grants and sample_grants, whose triggers on deleted_at remove them (migrations 41, 43, 44). Nothing reads a consent of a deleted artifact today; a trigger here would also have to be built in adoption's in-memory copy (migrations.rs jobs_tables_disagree), which has no artifacts table.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1329},"end":{"line":1342},"content_hash":"99e101a6350f979603aa5112ae4c5ec49f8a169951c678222e665b71cfab2af0"},"summary":"agent_read_consents and draft_renders rows outlive a soft-deleted artifact","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.955189Z","id":"26bb0137aaff69d5c156c1699456eff1dba35b9a281b5e4fe5b2a3057d8fbb91","body":{"detail":"Failure: a running job asks question Q of session S (Store::ask_job_question moves it to waiting), then S ends: the reaper (Store::reap_sessions, system:ttl), the person (end_session_by_person) or the agent (end_session). every session end calls withdraw_session_questions (sessions.rs:1675), whose bulk UPDATE (WITHDRAW_SESSION, questions.rs:421) sets Q to withdrawn without close_question, so close_job_question_tx (jobs.rs:940) never runs: job_questions.outcome stays NULL, the job stays waiting, and every later PATCH to running lands in waiting again (may_move with waits = true, jobs.rs:121). Nothing can close Q any more (close_question answers question_closed). This breaks spec 2026-10-19-in-process-core-design §7.4 (waiting: 'a withdrawal stores its outcome and moves the job to running') and §8.1, and the claim of resolve 8ee612dd that every ending close is stored.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":518},"end":{"line":536},"content_hash":"d0a4029caadaa4ff18d323d2b748676cd16154f94bbe2f8985f80611273b7402"},"suggested_fix":"In withdraw_session_questions, after WITHDRAW_SESSION, call self.close_job_question_tx(tx, &k.id, &JobAnswer::Withdrawn) for each withdrawn key (its job moves back to running, its outcome stored, its Event::Job heard through the update hook). Test in jobs.rs: running job asks a question of session s, st.end_session(DAEMON, s), the job is running at rev + 1 with JobAnswer::Withdrawn. Check every other bulk UPDATE of questions.status the same way (WITHDRAW_HOOKS only touches source = 'hook', which ask_job_question refuses).","summary":"A session's end withdraws a job's ask question without storing its outcome, so the job waits forever","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.955668Z","id":"81029f45e07486eaffe2f5fdb42c1e18b93885dbecb504e7df0102b7586ee559","body":{"detail":"A final job (cancelled or done) never reads an outcome again, so a question left open is one the person can answer for nothing, and its close is then stored nowhere (close_job_question_tx returns None for a final job). The final moves are three: patch_job to cancelled (jobs.rs:698), artifact_going_tx (jobs.rs:987) and commit_step with done (jobs.rs:859; may_move lets a waiting job's last step end it). stopped and failed are not final: Keep going and Retry move them back to running, which lands in waiting while the question is open, so the person's later answer is still used; withdrawing there would lose it. With the fix, no committed row holds a final job with a job_questions row whose outcome is NULL.","kind":"comment","references":"a750112f6d12a22d29bc78e73a1a127476ccc120bf00b895496c0f152b524f85","suggested_fix":"Factor close_question's Close::Withdraw arm (questions.rs CLOSE, record_question with a new Reason such as job_ended, inbox::question_changed) into withdraw_question_in(tx, ctx, qid, reason). Give jobs.rs one helper, ending(tx, job_id) called whenever moving() or may_move yields a state that is_final, that withdraws each SELECT question_id FROM job_questions WHERE job_id = ?1 AND outcome IS NULL through it and sets outcome = 'withdrawn'. patch_job and commit_step use AuditCtx::DAEMON (or gain a ctx), artifact_going_tx its caller's. Tests: cancel a waiting job, its question is withdrawn and its inbox item read; delete its artifact, the same; a done step on a waiting job, the same.","summary":"Yes: every move of a job to a final state should withdraw its unclosed questions in the same transaction; stopped, failed and paused should not","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.955936Z","id":"625ab7965401353e3eb52a878e5912851da3e7aa756a950ad7cd101d9eb83cde","body":{"detail":"A soft-deleted artifact is never purged in normal use: delete_corrupt_deleted_rows (artifacts.rs:633) removes only corrupt rows, and there is no undelete, so these rows stay for good, not until a purge. Store::agent_read_consents (jobs.rs:893) lists them with no deleted_at filter, so GET /api/agent-read-consents will show consents naming deleted artifacts. A trigger on artifacts, as migrations 41, 43 and 44 do, cannot be built by adoption's in-memory copy (jobs_tables_disagree executes migration 46 on a database with no artifacts table) and is not compared by it (it reads only tables and indexes). artifact_going_tx already runs inside every delete of an artifact, the soft delete included.","kind":"comment","references":"b5d2b6fa2bc784fc54b6c1b62bc9075235c75f6e23c5e0f75af8470325682359","suggested_fix":"In artifact_going_tx, after cancelling the jobs: DELETE FROM agent_read_consents WHERE reader = ?1 OR source = ?1; DELETE FROM draft_renders WHERE draft_id = ?1. Migration 46 is unchanged. Test: put consents both ways and a render for an artifact, delete_artifact it, agent_read_consents() and draft_renders are empty.","summary":"Remove them at the soft delete, in artifact_going_tx, rather than with a trigger","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.956141Z","id":"4240683dbddc51ab93a25c3232c0a2705f039c61916c768131e5abc99b03d43e","body":{"detail":"jobs_tables_disagree selects sqlite_master rows WHERE tbl_name = ?1 AND type IN ('table', 'index'). A trigger on jobs, job_steps or any other jobs table (an extra one in an earlier database, or one migration 46 later gains and an earlier database lacks) is neither required nor refused, though it changes what writes do. No text of migration 46 has had a trigger so far (git log -p of tests/fixtures/old-migrations/flutter-app-adbfc62df.sql), so no database is mis-adopted today. The normaliser itself is sound: SQLite keeps the CREATE text verbatim on every version, so an identical schema is never refused, and only spacing next to parentheses and commas, runs of spaces and -- comments are dropped, which cannot merge two tokens.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1631},"end":{"line":1636},"content_hash":"1b1bf31d09d8ca14c10140ed104c554ed015c601fe52be0b74976a31813cdb23"},"suggested_fix":"type IN ('table', 'index', 'trigger'), with a case in a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused that adds a trigger on jobs.","summary":"Adoption's comparison of the jobs tables reads only tables and indexes, so a trigger on them is not seen","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T07:34:36.956224Z","id":"7fd10650304ae9bb467d2ceef3f71368911d9fdc14a20eeb196b87f999a1a66f","body":{"detail":"threads_going bumps rev and updated_at of every job with a job_threads row for the thread, final ones included, so a done or cancelled job changes after it ended and its listener hears an Event::Job for it. JobError::Moved's contract (jobs.rs:373) and spec §8.1's table say a final job is changed by no write. Harmless to the worker (it drops rows of jobs it has not loaded) but it breaks the invariant the rest of jobs.rs keeps.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1046},"end":{"line":1061},"content_hash":"1c3b8677de9f3941a2ae34db91b65db08f9c1a1c62e9f88f47cd3a63403a5304"},"suggested_fix":"Add AND state NOT IN ('cancelled', 'done') to the UPDATE; the DELETE of job_threads still takes every row. Test: a done job answering a thread keeps its rev when the thread is deleted.","summary":"A thread's delete moves the rev of cancelled and done jobs, which no write is to change","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/questions.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:09.667588Z","id":"d4ce82bbcd96b439747daa3bf8dfa27988dbc65f2f9f10b68f392ac6cacffb36","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:49c75a391","summary":"Fixed: every close of a question goes through Store::close_in (questions.rs), which calls close_job_question_tx; a session's end and the daemon's start withdraw each question by withdraw_question_in, and the bulk UPDATEs WITHDRAW_SESSION and WITHDRAW_HOOKS are gone. jobs::tests::a_sessions_end_withdraws_its_question_and_moves_the_job_back (end_session and reap_sessions: the job is running at rev + 1 with JobAnswer::Withdrawn) failed before (left: (Waiting, 3), right: (Running, 4)) and passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"26bb0137aaff69d5c156c1699456eff1dba35b9a281b5e4fe5b2a3057d8fbb91","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/jobs.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:09.955658Z","id":"31b44448b49d4e7dff1c1a10439c105cc4d0e12b96730af670b034fe9202b408","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:e3c9f8eef","summary":"Fixed: patch_job to cancelled, commit_step with done and artifact_going_tx call Store::ending (jobs.rs), which withdraws each job_questions question with outcome NULL by withdraw_question_in (reason job_end, system:daemon) in the same transaction; close_job_question_tx stores the outcome for a final job without moving it. jobs::tests::a_jobs_final_move_withdraws_its_open_questions (each final move empties the owner's open questions, stores Withdrawn, leaves the final row as the move made it; stopped, failed and paused keep the question open) failed before (left: 1, right: 0) and passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"a750112f6d12a22d29bc78e73a1a127476ccc120bf00b895496c0f152b524f85","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:19.872045Z","id":"b8edf73ae0b16533a93fc5bc613d70a1bc48bacbca2b3a8a0a57c87075db79e8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:5a58fa893","summary":"Fixed as reply 625ab796 says: artifact_going_tx (jobs.rs), which every delete of an artifact runs, the soft delete included, deletes agent_read_consents naming the artifact as reader or source and its draft_renders; migration 46 is unchanged. jobs::tests::a_soft_deleted_artifact_takes_its_consents_and_renders (delete_artifact leaves only the consent and render not naming it) failed before and passes: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"b5d2b6fa2bc784fc54b6c1b62bc9075235c75f6e23c5e0f75af8470325682359","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-store/src/migrations.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T08:13:20.146222Z","id":"acfe4a4385bb6a2203ea918dd024354fde47514f5cf0a2eca365141992749722","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:28283b98b","summary":"Fixed: jobs_tables_disagree (migrations.rs) reads type IN ('table', 'index', 'trigger') and compares each by name, kind and normalised SQL, none missing and none more. The new case in migrations::tests::a_database_whose_jobs_tables_disagree_is_refused (a trigger jobs_touched on jobs) was not refused before and is now, by name, leaving the home as it was: bazelisk test //crates/clax-store:clax_store_lib_test, 733 passed, 0 failed.","supersedes":"4240683dbddc51ab93a25c3232c0a2705f039c61916c768131e5abc99b03d43e","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
